    <bpmn:process id="W_W983" name="W983. Customer Roofing Material Calculator &amp; GI Sheet/Insulation Sizing Recommendation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests roofing material quantity calculation at store or via mobile app
Frequency: ~6,000–8,000 calculations/month chain-wide (~30–40/store/month)
Volume: 1–2 roof sections per calculation; average 1.4 sections
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Roofing Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W983 — Customer Roofing Material Calculator &amp; GI Sheet/Insulation Sizing Recommendation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W983_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W983_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W983_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W983_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W983_Start4" name="Customer requests roofing material quantity calculation at store or via mobile app">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W983_Task5" name="Roof Measurement &amp; Structure Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Roof Measurement &amp; Structure Intake: Customer provides roof details via: (a) physical measurements — length and width of each roof section (in meters or feet), roof pitch/slope angle (or rise-over-run), number of valleys, hips, ridges, and dormers; (b) house floor plan or blueprint — Sales Associate interprets roof plan dimensions; (c) mobile app — customer uses BuildRight app&#x27;s roof measurement tool with satellite imagery overlay or AR measurement for existing structures; Sales Associate records: roof shape (gable, hip, shed, flat, combination), number of sections, pitch angle, overhang dimensions (typically 0.6–1.2m in PH residential), existing roof condition (new construction vs. re-roofing)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W983_Task6" name="Material Selection &amp; Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material Selection &amp; Specification: Customer selects roofing material with Sales Associate guidance: (a) GI sheet type — plain corrugated (longest life), pre-painted corrugated (colored, aesthetic), ribbed/standing seam (commercial); (b) gauge/thickness — Gauge 26 (0.45mm, economy residential), Gauge 24 (0.50mm, standard), Gauge 22 (0.63mm, premium/typhoon-rated); (c) length — 6ft, 8ft, 10ft, 12ft standard; custom lengths available via W988 welding/fabrication partner; (d) color (pre-painted only) — tile red, brick red, forest green, ocean blue, brown, white, beige; (e) insulation type — reflective foil (economy), foil-backed foam board (standard), fiberglass blanket (premium); (f) accessories — ridge cap, apex cap, valley flashing, gutter system, fascia cover, bargeboard, roofing screws with EPDM washers, butyl tape sealant
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W983_Task7" name="Automated Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Automated Quantity Calculation: System computes: (a) total roof area per section (plan area ÷ cos(pitch angle) for sloped surfaces); (b) effective coverage per sheet (gross sheet width minus side overlap of 1.5–2 corrugations ≈ 57–61 cm effective width; effective length = sheet length minus end overlap of 15–30 cm based on pitch); (c) sheets required per section = (roof width ÷ effective sheet width) × (roof slope length ÷ effective sheet length), rounded up to full sheets; (d) ridge cap pieces (linear meters of ridge ÷ cap coverage per piece); (e) valley flashing (linear meters of valleys ÷ effective flashing overlap); (f) insulation area = total roof area (same as sheet plan coverage, no overlap reduction); (g) screws = 12–16 per sheet (depending on purlin spacing); (h) gutter length = total eave perimeter; (i) total weight estimate for delivery planning (GI sheet ≈ 4–6 kg/sqm depending on gauge)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–4 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W983_Task8" name="Cross-Sell Accessories &amp; Services">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-Sell Accessories &amp; Services: Sales Associate recommends: (a) roof insulation (most customers skip this but it reduces indoor temperature by 3–5°C in PH tropical climate); (b) gutter system with downspouts (for rainwater collection, increasingly popular in PH); (c) fascia boards and bargeboard (weatherproofing roof edges); (d) roof installation service referral per W138; (e) waterproof roof sealant for nail/screw holes and overlaps; (f) safety equipment rental per W139 (safety harness, roofing brackets) for DIY customers; system updates quotation with all recommended accessories
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W983_Task9" name="Customer Review, Order Creation &amp; Delivery Scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer Review, Order Creation &amp; Delivery Scheduling: Customer reviews itemized materials list with quantities and prices; Sales Associate creates POS quotation per W542 or direct sale; for large orders (≥20 sheets or ≥200 kg total weight): (a) system schedules delivery via W5D or W980; (b) customer selects delivery date and confirms delivery address; (c) unloading assistance offered (roofing bundles require 2-person carry); (d) for orders exceeding store stock, system initiates inter-store transfer per W22 or DC replenishment per W4; quotation saved to customer&#x27;s loyalty account per W894 (Project Vault)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W983_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W983_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W983_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W983_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must prioritize same-batch allocation; operational: for roofing orders
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W983_Assoc12" sourceRef="W983_Annotation11" targetRef="W983_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow13" sourceRef="W983_Start4" targetRef="W983_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow14" sourceRef="W983_Task5" targetRef="W983_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow15" sourceRef="W983_Task6" targetRef="W983_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow16" sourceRef="W983_Task7" targetRef="W983_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow17" sourceRef="W983_Task8" targetRef="W983_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W983_Flow18" sourceRef="W983_Task9" targetRef="W983_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W983_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W983_plane" bpmnElement="W_W983">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W983_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W983_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W983_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W983_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W983_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W983_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W983_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W983_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_End10_di" bpmnElement="W983_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W983_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W983_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W983_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W983_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W983_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W984" name="W984. Customer Water Tank &amp; Pump System Sizing Recommendation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests water tank and/or pump sizing recommendation at store or via mobile app
Frequency: ~3,000–4,000 consultations/month chain-wide (~15–20/store/month)
Volume: 1 system per consultation; average 1 system
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W984 — Customer Water Tank &amp; Pump System Sizing Recommendation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W984_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W984_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W984_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W984_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W984_Start4" name="Customer requests water tank and/or pump sizing recommendation at store or via mobile app">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W984_Task5" name="Customer Water Demand Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Water Demand Assessment: Sales Associate collects: (a) number of household/establishment occupants; (b) number of bathrooms, kitchen sinks, laundry areas, and garden taps; (c) number of floors in the building (affects pump head pressure requirement); (d) water source — municipal supply (with pressure/volume issues), shallow well (≤25ft depth), deep well (&gt;25ft); (e) current water supply schedule (24/7, specific hours, intermittent); (f) available tank installation space (ground level, roof deck, inside utility room); (g) budget range
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W984_Task6" name="Tank Sizing Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tank Sizing Calculation: System calculates recommended tank capacity: (a) daily water consumption = occupants × 150 liters/person/day (PH standard residential); commercial/industrial uses higher factors; (b) desired storage days = 1–3 days for municipal supply backup, 1 day minimum for well systems; (c) tank capacity = daily consumption × storage days; (d) system recommends standard tank sizes (200L, 500L, 1000L, 2000L, 3000L, 5000L, 10000L) rounding up to nearest available size; (e) tank material recommendation — polyethylene (lightweight, UV-stabilized, economy), stainless steel (durable, hygienic, premium); (f) installation type — freestanding (ground level), elevated platform (roof deck), horizontal/vertical orientation based on available space
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W984_Task7" name="Pump Sizing &amp; Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pump Sizing &amp; Selection: System calculates pump specification: (a) required flow rate (liters per minute) based on simultaneous fixture usage (typically 2–3 fixtures simultaneously in residential); (b) total dynamic head (TDH) = vertical lift (suction head + discharge head to highest fixture) + friction loss (pipe length × friction factor per pipe diameter); (c) pump type recommendation — shallow well jet pump (depth ≤25ft, PH most common), deep well submersible pump (depth &gt;25ft), pressure booster pump (municipal supply with low pressure), automatic pump with pressure tank (for consistent pressure without cycling); (d) horsepower rating — 0.5HP (1-story, 1 bathroom), 1HP (2-story, 2–3 bathrooms), 1.5HP (large residential/commercial), 2HP+ (commercial/industrial); (e) power supply consideration — single-phase 220V (residential) vs. three-phase (commercial)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W984_Task8" name="Accessories &amp; Piping Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Accessories &amp; Piping Recommendation: System generates complete bill of materials: (a) PVC pipes (PVC schedule 40) — sizes based on flow rate (typically ¾&quot; to 1¼&quot; for residential); (b) fittings — elbows, tees, couplings, adapters, threaded connectors; (c) float valve (mechanical or electronic) for automatic tank refill; (d) gate valves/ball valves for isolation; (e) check valve (non-return) to prevent backflow; (f) pressure tank (for automatic pump systems — eliminates pump cycling); (g) pressure gauge and pressure switch; (h) pump controller (automatic dry-run protection mandatory for well pumps); (i) electrical wiring, circuit breaker, and waterproof outdoor switch; (j) pipe sealant (Teflon tape, solvent cement); (k) flexible connector hoses; (l) water filter (sediment filter recommended for well systems)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W984_Task9" name="Customer Review, Quotation &amp; Service Referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer Review, Quotation &amp; Service Referral: Customer reviews complete system recommendation with itemized pricing; Sales Associate: (a) presents total system cost and per-item breakdown; (b) offers installation service referral per W138 (plumber installation for complete system); (c) offers pipe cutting and threading service per W944 for custom pipe lengths; (d) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 14 days; (e) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894; (f) for well pump installations: advises customer on NWRB well permit requirements and recommends licensed well driller referral
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W984_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W984_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W984_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W984_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: for tanks above 500L; operational: recommendation, and installation referral — not lowest price on individual items
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
