    <bpmn:process id="W_W985" name="W985. Store-Level Customer Aircon Sizing &amp; BTU/Horsepower Calculation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests aircon sizing recommendation at store appliance section or via mobile app
Frequency: ~8,000–10,000 calculations/month chain-wide (~40–50/store/month); peaks March–May (PH summer)
Volume: 1–3 rooms per consultation; average 1.6 rooms
Owner: Department Supervisor (Home Appliances)
Participants: Sales Associate (Appliance Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W985 — Store-Level Customer Aircon Sizing &amp; BTU/Horsepower Calculation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W985_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W985_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W985_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W985_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W985_Start4" name="Customer requests aircon sizing recommendation at store appliance section or via mobile…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W985_Task5" name="Room Assessment &amp; Data Collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Room Assessment &amp; Data Collection: Sales Associate collects room parameters: (a) room dimensions — length × width × ceiling height (meters); (b) room type — bedroom, living room, kitchen, office, commercial space; (c) window area and orientation — north/south/east/west facing; window type (jalousie, sliding, awning, fixed glass); glass type (clear, tinted, reflective); presence of curtains/blinds; (d) wall material — concrete hollow block (CHB, most common in PH), wood frame, gypsum board partition; (e) insulation — none (typical PH residential), foam panel, fiberglass; (f) room occupancy — number of people typically in room; (g) heat sources — direct sunlight exposure, number of heat-generating appliances (refrigerator, oven, computer, TV); (h) floor level — ground floor, upper floor, top floor (roof heat gain); (i) existing electrical capacity — dedicated circuit available? Amperage of circuit breaker?
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W985_Task6" name="BTU/HP Calculation &amp; Unit Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BTU/HP Calculation &amp; Unit Recommendation: System calculates: (a) base cooling load = room area (sqm) × 500 BTU/sqm (PH tropical baseline for typical residential); (b) adjustments — ceiling height &gt; 2.7m (+10%), west-facing window (+10%), large window area &gt; 40% of wall (+10%), kitchen/heat sources (+4,000 BTU), top floor under roof (+15%), poor insulation (+10%); each occupant beyond first (+600 BTU); (c) total required BTU = base load + adjustments; (d) recommended unit size — 0.5HP/5,000BTU (small bedroom ≤10sqm), 0.75HP/7,000BTU (bedroom 10–14sqm), 1HP/9,000–10,000BTU (bedroom 14–18sqm), 1.5HP/12,000BTU (master bedroom/living room 18–25sqm), 2HP/18,000BTU (living room 25–35sqm), 2.5HP/24,000BTU (large living room 35–50sqm), cassette/duct type ≥3HP (commercial); (e) unit type recommendation — window type (economy, easy installation, typical PH), split type (inverter, quieter, more efficient), portable (rental/temporary), floor-mounted (large rooms), cassette/duct (commercial); (f) inverter vs. conventional recommendation — inverter recommended for rooms used ≥8 hours/day (bedrooms, offices); conventional acceptable for intermittent use (living rooms, guest rooms)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W985_Task7" name="Electrical Compatibility Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Electrical Compatibility Check: Sales Associate verifies: (a) required electrical load — unit wattage (typically 700W–2,500W depending on HP rating); (b) customer&#x27;s circuit breaker amperage — standard PH residential circuit is 20A/30A; (c) dedicated circuit requirement — units ≥1.5HP require dedicated circuit; (d) wiring gauge — units ≥1HP require 2.0mm² AWG14 wire minimum; ≥2HP require 3.5mm² AWG12; (e) Meralco/utility provider demand — some areas have limited residential electrical capacity; (f) system flags if customer&#x27;s electrical infrastructure is incompatible and recommends licensed electrician referral per W989
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W985_Task8" name="Cross-Sell Accessories &amp; Services">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-Sell Accessories &amp; Services: Sales Associate recommends: (a) aircon installation service per W138 (professional installation with copper piping, drainage hose, and electrical connection); (b) wall bracket/concealed mount for split-type outdoor unit; (c) aircon cover (off-season protection during Nov–Feb when usage drops); (d) air filter replacement schedule (clean monthly, replace quarterly); (e) voltage regulator/AVR (recommended for areas with unstable voltage — common in provincial PH); (f) drain hose and condensate pump (for units without gravity drainage); (g) extended warranty registration per W935; (h) electrical supplies per W991 (wiring, circuit breaker, outlet) if customer needs electrical upgrade
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W985_Task9" name="Quotation &amp; Order Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation &amp; Order Processing: Customer reviews recommendations; Sales Associate: (a) presents total cost including unit, accessories, and installation; (b) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 7 days (aircon pricing is volatile during summer peak); (c) for split-type units: coordinates installation scheduling per W138 with 2–5 day lead time; (d) for window-type units: customer may self-install or request installation service; (e) processes sale or saves quotation to customer loyalty account per W894; (f) system registers unit serial number at POS for warranty activation per W33
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W985_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W985_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W985_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W985_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Home Appliances) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Home Appliances)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W985_Assoc12" sourceRef="W985_Annotation11" targetRef="W985_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow13" sourceRef="W985_Start4" targetRef="W985_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow14" sourceRef="W985_Task5" targetRef="W985_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow15" sourceRef="W985_Task6" targetRef="W985_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow16" sourceRef="W985_Task7" targetRef="W985_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow17" sourceRef="W985_Task8" targetRef="W985_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W985_Flow18" sourceRef="W985_Task9" targetRef="W985_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W985_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W985_plane" bpmnElement="W_W985">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W985_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W985_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W985_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W985_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W985_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W985_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W985_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W985_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_End10_di" bpmnElement="W985_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W985_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W985_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W985_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W985_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W985_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W987" name="W987. Customer Fence &amp; Gate Material Estimation &amp; Design Recommendation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests fence/gate material estimation at store or via mobile app
Frequency: ~3,500–4,500 estimations/month chain-wide (~17–22/store/month)
Volume: 1 fence/gate project per estimation; average perimeter 30–80 linear meters
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Steel/Hardware Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W987 — Customer Fence &amp; Gate Material Estimation &amp; Design Recommendation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W987_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W987_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W987_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W987_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W987_Start4" name="Customer requests fence/gate material estimation at store or via mobile app">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W987_Task5" name="Project Scope &amp; Site Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Scope &amp; Site Intake: Customer provides project details: (a) total fence perimeter (linear meters); (b) fence height (typical PH residential: 1.8m–2.4m); (c) fence type — CHB hollow block wall, steel picket/tubular, welded wire mesh on steel frame, pre-painted corrugated on steel frame, chain-link, or combination; (d) gate requirements — number of gates, gate opening width (pedestrian: 1.0–1.2m, vehicle: 3.0–5.0m), gate type (swing single, swing double, sliding); (e) ground conditions — flat, sloped, rocky (affects footing depth and concrete volume); (f) existing structures — retaining walls, existing posts; (g) style/aesthetic preference (decorative spear tops, flat top, arch top)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W987_Task6" name="Material Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material Quantity Calculation: System calculates: (a) posts — steel tubular posts (2&quot; round or square) spaced at 2.0–2.5m centers; post count = perimeter ÷ spacing + 1; gate posts use heavier 3&quot; or 4&quot; tubular; post length = fence height + 0.6m footing depth; (b) horizontal rails — 2–3 runs per fence section (bottom, middle, top) in steel tubular (1&quot; round or 1½&quot; rectangular); total rail length = perimeter × number of runs; (c) infill material — steel pickets (quantity = section length ÷ picket spacing, typically 10–15cm); or CHB (blocks per sqm ≈ 12.5 for standard 8&quot;×16&quot;×4&quot; at 10mm joint); or welded wire mesh (rolls in 25m lengths × fence height); (d) concrete for footings — post footing volume (0.3m depth × 0.2m diameter × post count) + gate post footing (0.6m depth × 0.3m diameter × gate post count); (e) rebar for footings — 2–3 pieces of 12mm rebar per post footing; (f) gate frame — steel tubular frame sized to opening, cross-braced; (g) gate hardware — heavy-duty hinges (2–3 per gate), latch/lock set, drop bolt (for double gates), gate wheel (for sliding gates), guide track and rollers (for sliding gates); (h) paint/finish — primer + 2 coats enamel paint, estimated liters based on total steel surface area; (i) miscellaneous — cement (for CHB mortar), sand, tie wire, welding rods (if customer fabricates on-site), bolts and anchors
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W987_Task7" name="Gate Fabrication Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Gate Fabrication Recommendation: For custom steel gates: (a) system generates gate frame cutting list — top rail, bottom rail, vertical stiles, diagonal braces; (b) if customer has welding capability: provide material list only; (c) if customer needs fabricated gate: offer BuildRight&#x27;s welding/fabrication service per W988 with 3–5 day lead time; (d) gate design options — flat top, arch top, spear top (decorative), vertical bar, horizontal slat; (e) gate weight estimate for hinge/hardware selection
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W987_Task8" name="Cross-Sell Security &amp; Automation Accessories">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-Sell Security &amp; Automation Accessories: Sales Associate recommends: (a) padlock or mortise lock for gate (hardware section); (b) automatic gate operator (sliding or swing) for vehicle gates; (c) solar-powered gate operator (for areas without electrical access to gate); (d) CCTV camera at gate entrance per W207; (e) outdoor lighting (solar flood lights, sensor lights) for fence perimeter; (f) anti-climb devices for high-security applications; (g) paint color matching per W981 for fence/gate aesthetic coordination
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W987_Task9" name="Quotation &amp; Order Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation &amp; Order Processing: Customer reviews complete material list; Sales Associate: (a) presents itemized materials with quantities and pricing; (b) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 14 days; (c) for large orders (CHB, cement, sand, steel): schedules delivery per W5D or W980 for construction site delivery; (d) offers rebar cutting/bending service per W986 for footing reinforcement; (e) offers welding/fabrication service per W988 for gate fabrication; (f) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894; (g) for trade customers: quotation can be converted to project quotation per W162 for bid submission
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W987_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W987_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W987_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W987_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W987_Assoc12" sourceRef="W987_Annotation11" targetRef="W987_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
