    <bpmn:process id="W_W989" name="W989. Customer Plumbing System Layout Design &amp; Material Takeoff Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (homeowner, contractor, or plumber) requests plumbing layout design and material takeoff at store
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 consultations/month chain-wide (~10–15/store/month)
Volume: 1 project per consultation; ranges from single-bathroom renovation to full-house plumbing
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W989 — Customer Plumbing System Layout Design &amp; Material Takeoff Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W989_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W989_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W989_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W989_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W989_Start4" name="Customer (homeowner, contractor, or plumber) requests plumbing layout design and material…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W989_Task5" name="Project Scope &amp; Floor Plan Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Scope &amp; Floor Plan Intake: Customer provides: (a) floor plan — hand-drawn sketch, builder&#x27;s blueprint, or photo of floor plan showing fixture locations (toilet, lavatory, kitchen sink, shower, bathtub, washing machine, water heater, outdoor tap); (b) building type — single-story, two-story, three-story; (c) water source — municipal supply, water tank with pump per W984, deep well; (d) water heater type — tankless (point-of-use), storage tank (central), solar water heater; (e) project type — new construction, renovation (replacing existing plumbing), extension (adding bathroom/kitchen); (f) number of bathrooms, kitchen, laundry area, utility sink; Sales Associate marks fixture locations on system layout tool
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 12–18 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W989_Task6" name="Plumbing Layout Design &amp; Pipe Routing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Plumbing Layout Design &amp; Pipe Routing: System generates: (a) water supply layout — main supply line from source (typically 1&quot; PVC or PPR) branching to ¾&quot; lines to bathrooms and kitchen, then ½&quot; branches to individual fixtures; (b) drainage layout — 3&quot; or 4&quot; main drain line from toilets, 2&quot; from showers and sinks, with cleanout access points at code-required intervals; (c) vent layout — main vent stack (2&quot; minimum) through roof, with auxiliary vents per NPCP requirements (within 1.5m trap arm distance); (d) hot water supply routing (if water heater specified) — ½&quot; PPR or CPVC with insulated runs for energy efficiency; (e) fixture connection points — exact locations for shut-off valves, angle stops, P-traps, and supply adapters
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W989_Task7" name="Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation: System calculates complete bill of materials: (a) supply pipes — PVC schedule 40 or PPR (PN20), lengths by diameter (½&quot;, ¾&quot;, 1&quot;); (b) DWV pipes — PVC schedule 40, lengths by diameter (1½&quot;, 2&quot;, 3&quot;, 4&quot;); (c) fittings — elbows (90° and 45°), tees, couplings, reducers, adaptors, by pipe material and diameter; (d) valves — gate valves (main shut-off), angle stops (per fixture), check valves (if water pump per W984); (e) fixtures — toilets (close-coupled or wall-hung), lavatories, kitchen sinks, shower sets (per W997 compatibility check); (f) water heater and accessories per customer selection; (g) drain components — P-traps, sanitary tees, cleanouts, closet flanges; (h) sealants — solvent cement (PVC), Teflon tape, plumber&#x27;s putty, silicone sealant; (i) support/hangers — pipe clamps, brackets, stud anchors; (j) insulation — foam pipe insulation for hot water lines; (k) septic tank connection pipe and fittings (per W998 if new construction)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W989_Task8" name="Code Compliance Review &amp; Recommendations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Code Compliance Review &amp; Recommendations: Sales Associate reviews: (a) NPCP compliance — vent stack requirements, trap arm distances, pipe sizing adequacy, cleanout placement; (b) recommends upgrades — PPR over PVC for hot water lines (higher temperature rating), water hammer arrestors for washing machine/dishwasher connections, accessible shut-off valves for maintenance, backflow preventer if connected to municipal supply; (c) for multi-story buildings — pressure reducing valve may be needed for upper floors, booster pump per W984 for insufficient municipal pressure; (d) advises customer that plumbing layout is a material estimation aid, not a stamped engineering drawing; recommends licensed plumber for installation per W138
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W989_Task9" name="Quotation &amp; Order Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation &amp; Order Processing: Customer reviews complete material list with pricing; Sales Associate: (a) presents itemized materials grouped by category (supply, DWV, fixtures, accessories); (b) offers pipe cutting service per W944 for custom-length PVC/PPR pipes; (c) offers fixture compatibility check per W997 to ensure all bathroom/kitchen fixtures work together; (d) offers water tank/pump sizing per W984 if customer needs storage/distribution system; (e) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 14 days; (f) for large orders: schedules delivery per W5D for heavy/bulky items; (g) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W989_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W989_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W989_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W989_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: for building permit applications per LGU requirements per W54
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W989_Assoc12" sourceRef="W989_Annotation11" targetRef="W989_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow13" sourceRef="W989_Start4" targetRef="W989_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow14" sourceRef="W989_Task5" targetRef="W989_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow15" sourceRef="W989_Task6" targetRef="W989_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow16" sourceRef="W989_Task7" targetRef="W989_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow17" sourceRef="W989_Task8" targetRef="W989_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W989_Flow18" sourceRef="W989_Task9" targetRef="W989_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W989_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W989_plane" bpmnElement="W_W989">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W989_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W989_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
