    <bpmn:process id="W_W990" name="W990. Customer Solar Panel System Sizing &amp; ROI Calculator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquires about solar panel system at store or via mobile app
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 consultations/month chain-wide (~7–12/store/month); growing 30–40% annually
Volume: 1 system per consultation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Electrical)
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W990 — Customer Solar Panel System Sizing &amp; ROI Calculator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W990_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W990_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W990_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W990_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W990_Start4" name="Customer inquires about solar panel system at store or via mobile app">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W990_Task5" name="Energy Consumption Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Energy Consumption Assessment: Sales Associate collects: (a) average monthly electricity bill (PHP and kWh) — from customer&#x27;s utility bill; (b) peak monthly consumption (typically March–May due to aircon usage per W985); (c) electricity rate per kWh from utility; (d) roof type — metal GI sheet (most common in PH, easiest mounting), concrete slab, clay tile; (e) roof orientation — north-facing, south-facing (optimal in PH), east/west-facing, flat; (f) available roof area (sqm) — unshaded area between 9AM–3PM; (g) roof condition and structural adequacy for panel weight (~15 kg/m²); (h) building type — single-story residential, multi-story, commercial; (i) 3-phase or single-phase electrical supply
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W990_Task6" name="System Sizing Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System Sizing Calculation: System calculates: (a) system size (kWp) = monthly consumption (kWh) ÷ 30 days ÷ peak sun hours (4.5 for PH) ÷ system efficiency (0.75–0.80 derating factor for temperature, inverter, wiring losses); example: 500 kWh/month → 500 ÷ 30 ÷ 4.5 ÷ 0.77 ≈ 4.8 kWp system; (b) number of panels = system size ÷ panel wattage (500W panels: 4,800W ÷ 500W ≈ 10 panels); (c) required roof area = panels × panel area (2.0m² per 500W panel) = 20 sqm minimum; (d) inverter size = system size × 1.0–1.2 (slight oversizing for peak production); (e) annual energy production = system size × peak sun hours × 365 × derating = estimated kWh/year; (f) self-consumption ratio — estimated % of solar energy consumed directly vs. exported to grid; (g) battery sizing (optional hybrid system) = critical loads × desired backup hours
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W990_Task7" name="Financial ROI Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Financial ROI Analysis: System calculates: (a) total system cost = panels + inverter + mounting structure + electrical accessories + installation labor (per W138); (b) annual savings = annual production × self-consumption ratio × electricity rate + annual export × feed-in tariff; (c) simple payback period = total cost ÷ annual savings (typical PH residential: 4–6 years); (d) 25-year net savings = annual savings × 25 years × electricity rate escalation (3–5%/year assumed) − total cost − maintenance costs (inverter replacement at year 10–12); (e) internal rate of return (IRR); (f) comparison table: cash purchase vs. bank financing (partner bank per W966) with monthly amortization vs. monthly savings; (g) environmental impact — CO₂ avoided = annual production × 0.6 kg CO₂/kWh (PH grid emission factor)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W990_Task8" name="Product Selection &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Product Selection &amp; Quotation: Sales Associate presents: (a) system components — panels (Tier 1 brand recommendation), inverter (string inverter for simple roofs, micro-inverter for complex/shaded roofs), mounting kit, AC/DC disconnect, circuit breaker, cables and connectors; (b) optional battery bank for hybrid/off-grid capability; (c) total system cost with itemized pricing; (d) installation service referral per W138 with certified solar installer; (e) net metering application assistance — advise customer on utility net metering application process (BuildRight provides checklist and required technical documents but does not file the application); (f) LGU electrical permit requirements per W54; (g) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 30 days (solar equipment pricing is relatively stable)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W990_Task9" name="Documentation &amp; Follow-Up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Documentation &amp; Follow-Up: For customers who proceed: (a) system generates technical summary document with system specifications, layout diagram, and ROI analysis for customer&#x27;s records; (b) Sales Associate schedules site assessment per W442 (technical survey for roof condition, shading analysis, and electrical panel compatibility) before final installation commitment; (c) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894; (d) system registers follow-up task for Sales Associate to contact customer in 7 days if quotation not converted to sale; (e) for net metering customers: provides utility application checklist and list of required documents
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W990_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W990_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W990_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W990_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: before installation commitment; operational: output; operational: monitoring
Owner: Department Supervisor (Electrical)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W990_Assoc12" sourceRef="W990_Annotation11" targetRef="W990_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
