    <bpmn:process id="W_W991" name="W991. Customer Electrical Circuit Design &amp; Residential Load Planning Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests electrical circuit planning assistance for new construction or renovation
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 consultations/month chain-wide (~10–15/store/month)
Volume: 1 project per consultation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Electrical)
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W991 — Customer Electrical Circuit Design &amp; Residential Load Planning Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W991_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W991_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W991_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W991_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W991_Start4" name="Customer requests electrical circuit planning assistance for new construction or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W991_Task5" name="Building Assessment &amp; Load Inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Building Assessment &amp; Load Inventory: Sales Associate collects: (a) floor plan with room layout (hand-drawn or photo); (b) number of rooms and room types (bedrooms, living room, kitchen, bathrooms, garage, laundry); (c) planned appliances and equipment per room — aircon (per W985 with HP rating), water heater, electric stove/induction cooker, refrigerator, washing machine, microwave, water pump (per W984 with HP rating), lighting fixtures, number of convenience outlets per room; (d) building type — single-story, two-story; (e) service entrance — overhead or underground, existing panel amperage (typically 60A or 100A for PH residential); (f) project type — new construction, renovation, extension
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W991_Task6" name="Circuit Design &amp; Load Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Circuit Design &amp; Load Calculation: System designs circuits per PEC guidelines: (a) lighting circuits — 1 circuit per 800W of lighting load, 2.0mm² THHN wire (minimum), 15A circuit breaker; (b) convenience outlet circuits — 1 circuit per 6 outlets maximum, 2.0mm² THHN wire, 20A circuit breaker, GFCI protection for wet areas (bathrooms, kitchen, outdoor); (c) dedicated appliance circuits — aircon: 1 circuit per unit, 3.5mm² THHN for 1HP, 5.5mm² THHN for 2HP, 30A circuit breaker; water heater: dedicated circuit, 3.5mm² THHN, 30A circuit breaker; electric stove: dedicated circuit, 8.0mm² THHN, 40–50A circuit breaker; water pump: dedicated circuit per W984 pump HP rating; (d) total connected load (watts) and computed load per PEC demand factors; (e) main breaker and panel size recommendation — 100A panel for standard residential, 200A for large residential with multiple aircon units; (f) service entrance wire size — based on computed load and distance from utility meter
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W991_Task7" name="Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation: System generates complete bill of materials: (a) wire — THHN/THWN copper wire by gauge (2.0mm², 3.5mm², 5.5mm², 8.0mm²) with estimated lengths per circuit × 1.15 waste factor; (b) circuit breakers — quantity and amperage per circuit design, including main breaker; (c) panel board — load center with sufficient breaker slots; (d) conduit — PVC conduit or EMT by diameter with fittings; (e) junction boxes — quantity by type (round, square, octagonal); (f) switches — single-pole, 3-way, 4-way by quantity per room; (g) outlets/convenience outlets — standard, GFCI (wet areas), grounded, by quantity; (h) connectors and accessories — wire nuts, cable ties, ground rod, ground wire, terminal lugs, EMT connectors, PVC cement, electrical tape; (i) safety devices — surge protector, AFCI breakers (recommended for bedrooms); (j) lighting fixtures — quantity per room (if customer selects)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W991_Task8" name="Code Compliance Review &amp; Safety Recommendations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Code Compliance Review &amp; Safety Recommendations: Sales Associate reviews: (a) PEC compliance — circuit breaker sizing, wire gauge adequacy, grounding requirements (8ft ground rod mandatory per PEC), GFCI placement in wet areas; (b) recommends safety upgrades — whole-house surge protector (critical in typhoon-prone PH with frequent lightning), AFCI breakers for bedrooms (arc fault protection), smoke detectors per floor, CO detector if gas appliances present; (c) advises customer that material list is a planning aid, not a professional electrical engineering design; recommends licensed electrician for installation per W138 and PEC compliance certification; (d) for renovation projects: advises on aluminum-to-copper transition safety and knob-and-tube wiring hazards (common in older PH homes)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W991_Task9" name="Quotation &amp; Order Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation &amp; Order Processing: Customer reviews complete material list; Sales Associate: (a) presents itemized materials grouped by circuit; (b) offers wire cutting service for custom-length wire runs; (c) offers lighting fixture selection per W997 for bathroom/kitchen fixture coordination; (d) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 14 days; (e) for large orders (full-house rewiring): schedules delivery per W5D for heavy items (panel, conduit, wire rolls); (f) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W991_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W991_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W991_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W991_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Electrical) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Electrical)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W991_Assoc12" sourceRef="W991_Annotation11" targetRef="W991_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow13" sourceRef="W991_Start4" targetRef="W991_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow14" sourceRef="W991_Task5" targetRef="W991_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow15" sourceRef="W991_Task6" targetRef="W991_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow16" sourceRef="W991_Task7" targetRef="W991_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow17" sourceRef="W991_Task8" targetRef="W991_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W991_Flow18" sourceRef="W991_Task9" targetRef="W991_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
