    <bpmn:process id="W_W993" name="W993. Customer Construction Project Timeline &amp; Phased Material Delivery Planner" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade/contractor customer requests phased material delivery planning for a construction project
Frequency: ~1,000–1,500 plans/month chain-wide (~5–7/store/month)
Volume: 1 project per plan; projects range from PHP 200,000 to PHP 5,000,000+ in total material purchases
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Desk), Customer (Contractor), Category Manager, Supply Chain Planner, Delivery Coordinator
Source: workflow W993 — Customer Construction Project Timeline &amp; Phased Material Delivery Planner</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W993_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W993_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W993_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W993_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W993_Start4" name="Trade/contractor customer requests phased material delivery planning for a construction…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W993_Task5" name="Project Scope &amp; Timeline Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Scope &amp; Timeline Intake: Contractor provides: (a) project type — residential (single-story, two-story), commercial, renovation; (b) project scope — floor area (sqm), number of floors, number of rooms/bathrooms; (c) estimated project duration — start date and target completion date; (d) construction method — CHB conventional (most common in PH), pre-fab, steel frame; (e) quality level — economy (basic finishes), standard (mid-range), premium (high-end); (f) project location and site access constraints (narrow street, no parking, height restrictions); (g) existing customer account or new trade account application per W24
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W993_Task6" name="Construction Phase Mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Construction Phase Mapping: System maps material requirements to construction phases: (a) Phase 1 — Foundation: rebar (per W986 cutting/bending), cement, sand, gravel, anchor bolts, formwork lumber, polyethylene sheeting (vapor barrier); (b) Phase 2 — Structural: CHB hollow blocks, cement, rebar, tie wire, structural steel beams, metal deck (if applicable); (c) Phase 3 — Roofing: GI sheets (per W983), purlins, ridge cap, insulation, roofing screws, gutters; (d) Phase 4 — Plumbing rough-in: PVC/PPR pipes, fittings, fixtures (per W989 layout), water tank (per W984); (e) Phase 5 — Electrical rough-in: wire, conduit, panel, breakers, boxes (per W991 design); (f) Phase 6 — Masonry &amp; Finishing: tiles (per W963), tile adhesive, grout, plaster, skim coat, paint (per W981 color matching); (g) Phase 7 — Fixtures &amp; Fittings: toilets, faucets, switches, outlets, doors, locks, cabinets; (h) Phase 8 — Final: appliances (aircon per W985), lighting, hardware, accessories
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W993_Task7" name="Delivery Schedule Optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Delivery Schedule Optimization: System generates delivery schedule: (a) assigns each phase a delivery date based on construction timeline (Phase 1: week 1, Phase 2: weeks 2–4, Phase 3: weeks 4–5, etc.); (b) groups small phases that can share a delivery truck (e.g., Phase 4 plumbing + Phase 5 electrical may overlap); (c) calculates delivery truck requirements per phase — weight, volume, and special handling (steel and cement require flatbed or 10-wheeler; tiles require covered truck); (d) identifies multi-drop opportunities for urban projects with limited on-site storage; (e) optimizes delivery route if multiple projects share delivery windows in same geographic area; (f) flags potential DC inventory constraints for imported materials (tiles, fixtures) with longer lead times
Responsible (R): System / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W993_Task8" name="Pricing, Payment Terms &amp; Contract">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pricing, Payment Terms &amp; Contract: Sales Associate presents: (a) total project material cost with per-phase breakdown; (b) price lock terms — pricing guaranteed for 60 days from contract signing (beyond 60 days: price adjustment clause for steel and cement which are commodity-priced); (c) payment terms — per-delivery payment (standard) or project credit facility per W24 for qualifying trade accounts; (d) deposit requirement — 20% of Phase 1 material cost to confirm project and reserve stock; (e) volume discount — if total project material cost exceeds PHP 500,000, tiered discount applied per trade pricing matrix per W163; (f) creates project quotation per W162 with phased delivery schedule as annex; (g) contractor signs delivery acceptance agreement
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W993_Task9" name="Order Execution &amp; Ongoing Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Order Execution &amp; Ongoing Coordination: After contract signing: (a) system creates blanket purchase order per customer with phased release triggers; (b) 3 days before each phase delivery date: system automatically sends reminder to contractor and confirms delivery; (c) contractor confirms or adjusts delivery date (±3 days flexibility); (d) system triggers DC pick/pack/ship per W106 for confirmed delivery; (e) on delivery day: driver calls contractor 30 minutes before arrival; goods receipt confirmed by contractor per W18; (f) system invoices delivered materials per phase; (g) after each phase delivery, Sales Associate follows up to confirm material adequacy and discuss next phase adjustments per W954
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Supply Chain Planner / Delivery Coordinator
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Ongoing (5–10 min per phase)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W993_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W993_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W993_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W993_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must handle date changes without losing price lock or stock reservation; operational: must have weather contingency logic and backup delivery dates
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W993_Assoc12" sourceRef="W993_Annotation11" targetRef="W993_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow13" sourceRef="W993_Start4" targetRef="W993_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow14" sourceRef="W993_Task5" targetRef="W993_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow15" sourceRef="W993_Task6" targetRef="W993_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow16" sourceRef="W993_Task7" targetRef="W993_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow17" sourceRef="W993_Task8" targetRef="W993_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W993_Flow18" sourceRef="W993_Task9" targetRef="W993_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W993_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W993_plane" bpmnElement="W_W993">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W993_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W993_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
