    <bpmn:process id="W_W997" name="W997. Customer Bathroom/Kitchen Fixture Compatibility Checker &amp; Bundle Builder" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer selects bathroom or kitchen fixtures and needs compatibility verification or wants to build a complete fixture bundle
Frequency: ~4,000–6,000 checks/month chain-wide (~20–30/store/month)
Volume: 1–3 fixtures per compatibility check; 1 complete bundle per bundle builder session
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing/Fixture Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W997 — Customer Bathroom/Kitchen Fixture Compatibility Checker &amp; Bundle Builder</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W997_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W997_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W997_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W997_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W997_Start4" name="Customer selects bathroom or kitchen fixtures and needs compatibility verification or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W997_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W997_Task5" name="Fixture Selection &amp; Compatibility Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fixture Selection &amp; Compatibility Check: Customer selects fixture(s) — toilet (close-coupled, wall-hung, floor-mounted, one-piece, two-piece), lavatory/basin (counter-top, under-mount, wall-hung, pedestal), faucet (single-hole, centerset, widespread, wall-mount), shower system (shower head + diverter + valve trim), kitchen sink (single bowl, double bowl, under-mount, top-mount), kitchen faucet (single-handle, pull-down, commercial style); Sales Associate enters selections into compatibility checker; system checks: (a) mounting compatibility — wall-hung basin requires wall-mount bracket and concealed carrier (if not existing); floor-mount toilet requires 10&quot; or 12&quot; rough-in distance matching existing waste pipe; (b) hole configuration — faucet hole spacing (single-hole, 4&quot; centerset, 8&quot; widespread) must match basin/sink drilling; (c) connection compatibility — faucet connections (flexible hose, rigid supply) must match customer&#x27;s supply valve type (angle stop, straight stop); (d) water pressure compatibility — low-pressure systems (gravity-fed tank per W984) may not work with high-flow shower heads; (e) pipe material compatibility — connection adapters needed if existing pipes are GI (galvanized iron) and new fixtures are threaded PVC/PPR
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W997_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W997_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W997_Task6" name="Compatibility Issue Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Compatibility Issue Resolution: For any incompatibilities detected: (a) system identifies specific issue (e.g., &quot;Selected faucet requires 8-inch widespread holes; selected basin has 4-inch centerset drilling&quot;); (b) system suggests compatible alternatives from same brand or equivalent brands at similar price point; (c) system identifies required adapters/connectors (e.g., GI-to-PPR adapter, reducing coupling, extender flange); (d) Sales Associate presents options to customer with clear explanation of why incompatibility exists and how alternatives resolve it; (e) for complex compatibility issues (mixed brands, older plumbing): Sales Associate recommends bringing photos of existing plumbing or visiting with measurements for accurate assessment
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W997_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W997_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W997_Task7" name="Bundle Builder — Complete Room Package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Bundle Builder — Complete Room Package: Customer opts for complete bundle; system presents pre-configured packages or builds custom: (a) Economy Bathroom Bundle (~PHP 8,000–12,000): close-coupled toilet, counter-top basin, single-hole faucet, shower head with diverter, angle stops, flexible connectors, toilet seat cover; (b) Standard Bathroom Bundle (~PHP 15,000–25,000): two-piece toilet (dual-flush), under-mount basin on vanity top, widespread faucet, rain shower head + handheld shower with diverter, complete accessories (towel bar, toilet paper holder, soap dish, toothbrush holder); (c) Premium Bathroom Bundle (~PHP 35,000–60,000): one-piece toilet (soft-close seat), designer basin on furniture vanity, sensor faucet, thermostatic shower system with body jets, premium accessories, LED mirror cabinet; (d) Kitchen Bundle (~PHP 10,000–40,000): double-bowl sink, pull-down faucet, soap dispenser, under-sink filtration system; (e) system calculates bundle price with 5–10% discount vs. individual item pricing
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W997_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W997_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W997_Task8" name="Quotation, Accessories &amp; Service Referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quotation, Accessories &amp; Service Referral: Customer reviews bundle; Sales Associate: (a) presents itemized bundle contents with individual and bundle pricing; (b) recommends additional items — bathroom/kitchen waterproofing membrane (per W963 tile calculator), mirror, exhaust fan, towel warmer, water heater per W985 (for bathroom); (c) offers plumbing layout design per W989 for complete room renovation; (d) offers installation service referral per W138 (plumber for fixture installation); (e) offers tile/flooring calculator per W963 for floor and wall tiles; (f) creates POS quotation per W542 valid for 14 days; (g) quotation saved to customer loyalty account per W894
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W997_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W997_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W997_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W997_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W997_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must track bundle components and apply proportional refund logic per W12
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W997_Assoc11" sourceRef="W997_Annotation10" targetRef="W997_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
