    <bpmn:process id="W_W1043" name="W1043. Customer Paint Coverage Area Calculator &amp; Primer/Finish Quantity Estimator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests paint quantity recommendation at paint mixing station, pro desk, or via ecommerce
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 customer interactions/month across all stores (paint is 8% of SKU portfolio, ~2,800 SKUs)
Volume: 1 estimation per customer visit; average 3–5 surface calculations per project
Owner: Paint Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Paint Section), Paint Mixing Station Operator, Customer
Source: workflow W1043 — Customer Paint Coverage Area Calculator &amp; Primer/Finish Quantity Estimator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1043_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1043_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1043_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1043_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1043_Start4" name="Customer requests paint quantity recommendation at paint mixing station, pro desk, or via…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1043_Task5" name="Customer Project Intake &amp; Surface Area Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Project Intake &amp; Surface Area Calculation: Sales Associate gathers project details: (a) surface type — interior wall, exterior wall, ceiling, trim/door, metal gate/railing, roof; (b) wall material — new CHB/concrete, old concrete (previously painted), drywall, plywood, wood, metal, stucco/roughcast; (c) surface condition — bare/unpainted, previously painted (good condition), previously painted (peeling/flaking), with stains/water marks; (d) room/area dimensions — length, width, height of each wall or surface; (e) deductions — window openings, door openings, built-in cabinets; (f) desired finish — flat, satin, semi-gloss, gloss; (g) system calculates net paintable surface area (gross area minus deductions) and applies surface-type absorption factor (CHB: 1.3–1.4×; smooth concrete: 1.0×; wood: 1.1×; metal: 0.9×)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Paint Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1043_Task6" name="Primer &amp; Undercoat Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Primer &amp; Undercoat Recommendation: System determines primer requirements: (a) new CHB/concrete surfaces: alkaline-resistant primer (mandatory, 1 coat); (b) previously painted surfaces in good condition: no primer needed unless changing from oil-based to water-based; (c) peeling/flaking surfaces: scraping + patching compound + primer (1 coat); (d) stained/water-marked surfaces: stain-blocking primer (1 coat); (e) metal surfaces: anti-rust primer (1 coat); (f) exterior surfaces: weather-resistant primer (1 coat); (g) system calculates primer volume using primer coverage rate (typically 30–40 sqm per gallon for Philippine brands) and surfaces requiring primer
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Paint Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1043_Task7" name="Finish Coat Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Finish Coat Quantity Calculation: System computes finish coat quantity: (a) number of coats recommended — interior walls: 2 coats; exterior walls: 2–3 coats (tropical rain exposure); ceiling: 2 coats; metal: 2 coats; (b) coverage rate per product — varies by paint line (economy: 25–30 sqm/gallon; premium: 35–45 sqm/gallon); system pulls coverage data from product master (W252) based on selected paint SKU; (c) total volume = (net surface area × absorption factor × number of coats) ÷ coverage rate per gallon; (d) system rounds up to nearest gallon/4-liter container and adds 10% contingency for touch-ups; (e) if customer has selected paint color, system checks availability in required volume per real-time inventory (W11/W533)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Paint Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1043_Task8" name="Ancillary Supplies Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Ancillary Supplies Recommendation: System generates companion product list: (a) paint rollers — 7&quot; or 9&quot; width based on wall area; roller covers (nap length: 3/8&quot; smooth, 1/2&quot;–3/4&quot; rough surfaces); (b) paint brushes — 2&quot; trim brush, 4&quot; wall brush; (c) paint tray and liners; (d) masking tape (painter&#x27;s tape) — 1&quot; and 2&quot; widths, calculated linear meters based on edge/trim length; (e) sandpaper — grit 120 (surface prep), grit 220 (between coats); (f) putty/spackling knife and patching compound for surface repair; (g) drop cloth/plastic sheeting — sized to room dimensions; (h) solvent/cleaner — water for latex, mineral spirits for oil-based; (i) system bundles these as a &quot;project supply kit&quot; with total estimated cost
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1043_Task9" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/pdf estimate with: project summary (room name, dimensions, surface types), calculated paintable area, primer recommendation (brand, product, volume, coats), finish coat recommendation (brand, product, color code, volume, coats), ancillary supply list with quantities and prices, total estimated project cost, estimated project time (drying time between coats: 2–4 hours water-based, 6–8 hours oil-based in Philippine humidity); (b) estimate saved to customer&#x27;s loyalty account or as guest session; (c) customer can directly convert estimate to in-store transaction by scanning estimate QR code at POS (W542); (d) for trade account customers, estimate can be saved as project quote per W542 with 30-day validity; (e) paint mixing station operator receives color formula and volume — proceeds to W168 (custom paint mixing) if customer confirms
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Paint Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1043_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1043_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1043_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1043_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: should recommend rounding up and note this risk on the estimate
Owner: Paint Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1043_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1043_Annotation11" targetRef="W1043_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1043_Flow13" sourceRef="W1043_Start4" targetRef="W1043_Task5" />
