    <bpmn:process id="W_W1044" name="W1044. Customer Concrete Mix Ratio &amp; Volume Calculator for Slab/Foundation/Column Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests concrete quantity estimate for a construction project (slab, footing, column, beam, driveway, post filler)
Frequency: ~4,000–6,000 customer interactions/month across all stores (cement and concrete materials are in the lumber &amp; building materials category — 14% of SKUs)
Volume: 1 calculation per customer project
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1044 — Customer Concrete Mix Ratio &amp; Volume Calculator for Slab/Foundation/Column Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1044_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1044_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1044_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1044_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1044_Start4" name="Customer requests concrete quantity estimate for a construction project (slab, footing…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1044_Task5" name="Project Type &amp; Structural Element Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Type &amp; Structural Element Identification: Sales Associate identifies the concrete application: (a) slab-on-grade (floor slab, driveway, carport); (b) footing/foundation (isolated footing, continuous footing, mat foundation); (c) column (rectangular, circular); (d) beam (tie beam, grade beam, lintel); (e) wall (CHB wall footings, retaining wall); (f) post filler (hollow block post filler, 4&quot;/6&quot; round column filler); (g) stairs; (h) other custom form. System displays the applicable structural standards and minimum recommended concrete class (Class A for structural, Class B for general, Class C for fill)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1044_Task6" name="Dimension Input &amp; Volume Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Dimension Input &amp; Volume Calculation: Customer provides dimensions and system computes volume: (a) rectangular slab: length × width × thickness (in meters; default thickness: 0.10m for residential floor, 0.15m for garage/driveway); (b) L-shaped or irregular slab: decomposed into rectangles; (c) footing: length × width × depth (typical depth 0.60–1.20m for single-story); (d) column: width × depth × height; (e) circular column: π × radius² × height; (f) beam: width × depth × length; (g) retaining wall: length × height × thickness (tapers if applicable); (h) system adds waste factor: 5% for simple shapes, 10% for irregular shapes or complex formwork; (i) system outputs total concrete volume in cubic meters (m³)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer / System
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1044_Task7" name="Mix Design &amp; Material Quantity Breakdown">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Mix Design &amp; Material Quantity Breakdown: System computes material quantities based on selected mix class: (a) Class A (1:2:4): ~9.0–9.5 bags cement per m³, 0.67 m³ sand, 1.33 m³ gravel; (b) Class B (1:2½:5): ~7.0–7.5 bags cement per m³, 0.70 m³ sand, 1.40 m³ gravel; (c) Class C (1:3:6): 5.0 bags cement per m³, 0.83 m³ sand per m³, 1.67 m³ gravel per m³; (d) system multiplies per-m³ quantities by total volume (including waste factor); (e) outputs: number of cement bags (40 kg), volume of sand (m³ or cubic meters equivalent in truck loads), volume of gravel (m³ or cubic meters equivalent in truck loads), estimated water volume (liters); (f) for projects &gt;3 m³, system recommends ready-mixed concrete as an alternative per W964 (bulk delivery) and shows cost comparison: bagged DIY vs. ready-mix delivered
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1044_Task8" name="Companion Materials Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Companion Materials Recommendation: System generates companion product list: (a) reinforcing steel (rebar) — size and quantity per standard spacing (10mm @ 200mm O.C. for slab; 12mm or 16mm for columns and beams) per W986/W1060; (b) tie wire — 1.5 kg per 100 kg of rebar; (c) formwork materials — plywood (1/4&quot; or 1/2&quot; for concrete forming), 2×2 or 2×3 wood studs for form support; (d) plastic sheeting — for curing cover (kept wet for 7 days per Philippine engineering practice); (e) vibro-tamping rod or concrete vibrator rental per W139; (f) wheelbarrow and mixing tools; (g) waterproofing compound for below-grade concrete; (h) system bundles companion materials with total estimated cost
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1044_Task9" name="Estimate Generation, Delivery Scheduling &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Estimate Generation, Delivery Scheduling &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/PDF estimate with: project description, structural element dimensions, computed concrete volume, selected mix class with ratio, material quantity breakdown (cement bags, sand m³, gravel m³, water liters), companion materials list with prices, total estimated project cost; (b) for orders &gt;2 m³ of sand/gravel: system triggers bulk delivery scheduling per W964 with delivery fee estimate based on distance; (c) for orders ≤2 m³: customer can load materials at store yard per W950 (vehicle loading assistance); (d) estimate saved to customer&#x27;s loyalty account; (e) customer can convert estimate to transaction at POS per W542; (f) for trade account B2B customers, estimate converts to project quote per W162 with delivery window scheduling
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1044_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1044_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1044_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1044_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: should note this on estimates
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1044_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1044_Annotation11" targetRef="W1044_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow13" sourceRef="W1044_Start4" targetRef="W1044_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow14" sourceRef="W1044_Task5" targetRef="W1044_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow15" sourceRef="W1044_Task6" targetRef="W1044_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow16" sourceRef="W1044_Task7" targetRef="W1044_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow17" sourceRef="W1044_Task8" targetRef="W1044_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1044_Flow18" sourceRef="W1044_Task9" targetRef="W1044_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1044_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1044_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1044">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_End10_di" bpmnElement="W1044_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1044_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1044_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W1044_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1048" name="W1048. Customer Rainwater Harvesting System Design &amp; Material Sizing Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests rainwater harvesting system design, or expresses interest in water conservation during plumbing/building materials consultation
Frequency: ~500–800 consultations/month across all stores (growing interest in Philippine water conservation, especially in water-scarce regions like Metro Manila, Cebu, and parts of Mindanao)
Volume: 1 system design per customer consultation
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1048 — Customer Rainwater Harvesting System Design &amp; Material Sizing Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1048_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1048_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1048_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1048_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1048_Start4" name="Customer requests rainwater harvesting system design, or expresses interest in water…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1048_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1048_Task5" name="Catchment Area &amp; Demand Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Catchment Area &amp; Demand Assessment: Sales Associate gathers project parameters: (a) roof type — galvanized iron (GI) sheet, clay tile, concrete flat roof, metal deck; (b) roof catchment area — length × width of roof section(s) that will drain to the collection system (in square meters); (c) roof slope and gutter location; (d) average annual rainfall for customer&#x27;s location (system auto-populates from PAGASA data based on customer&#x27;s city/municipality per W310 — address hierarchy); (e) water demand — intended uses (garden/lawn irrigation, toilet flushing, laundry, car washing, general cleaning); (f) available space for storage tank (ground level, elevated platform, underground); (g) existing gutter system — compatible or needs replacement; (h) budget range
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1048_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1048_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1048_Task6" name="Storage Tank Sizing Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Storage Tank Sizing Calculation: System computes recommended tank capacity: (a) monthly harvestable rainwater (liters/month) = roof catchment area (m²) × average monthly rainfall (mm) × 0.85 (runoff coefficient for GI/metal roof; 0.75 for concrete; 0.80 for tile) × 0.90 (first-flush diverter and filter losses); (b) system displays monthly harvest by month using PAGASA rainfall distribution (wet months June–November produce 70–80% of annual harvest); (c) recommended tank size = 2–3 months of dry-season demand (December–May) to bridge the dry period; (d) system recommends tank model(s) from inventory: 500L (small household, garden only), 1,000L (medium household, garden + toilet flushing), 2,000L–5,000L (large household or small commercial), 10,000L (commercial/institutional); (e) system checks real-time inventory (W533) for recommended tank at customer&#x27;s store
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1048_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1048_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1048_Task7" name="System Component Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System Component Specification: System generates complete bill of materials: (a) gutter system — PVC or aluminum gutter (125mm or 150mm half-round or box profile), length = roof perimeter along collection side, brackets @ 600mm O.C., end caps, joiners; (b) downspout(s) — PVC pipe diameter (75mm or 100mm), number of downspouts (1 per 50 sqm of roof area, minimum 2), elbows and brackets; (c) first-flush diverter — 1 per downspout (diverts first 20 liters of rainwater containing roof contaminants); (d) leaf screen / mesh filter — installed at gutter-to-downspout transition; (e) inlet filter — at tank entry point; (f) storage tank — per step 2 recommendation; (g) overflow pipe — PVC pipe from tank overflow to storm drain, diameter ≥ downspout diameter; (h) outlet fitting — ball valve or float valve at tank base; (i) pump (optional) — submersible pump per W984 sizing if customer needs pressurized output; (j) pipework from tank to point-of-use — PVC pipe, fittings, isolation valves; (k) system calculates total material cost using current pricing per W252
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1048_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1048_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1048_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/PDF estimate with: project summary (roof area, location, rainfall data), monthly harvest calculation with PAGASA data table, recommended tank size with rationale, complete bill of materials with quantities and prices, total estimated system cost, estimated installation time (DIY: 1–2 days; professional: 4–6 hours), maintenance requirements (gutter cleaning quarterly, tank cleaning annually, filter replacement as needed); (b) if tank requires delivery (tanks &gt;500L): system triggers home delivery scheduling per W5D with delivery fee estimate; (c) offer professional installation referral per W138 (home installation services) and W904 (contractor referral); (d) estimate saved to customer&#x27;s loyalty account; (e) customer can convert estimate to POS transaction per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1048_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1048_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1048_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1048_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1048_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
