    <bpmn:process id="W_W1050" name="W1050. Customer Staircase Tread, Riser &amp; Railing Material Calculator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests staircase material quantities for residential or small commercial construction project
Frequency: ~800–1,200 consultations/month across all stores
Volume: 1 staircase calculation per consultation
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1050 — Customer Staircase Tread, Riser &amp; Railing Material Calculator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1050_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1050_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1050_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1050_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1050_Start4" name="Customer requests staircase material quantities for residential or small commercial…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1050_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1050_Task5" name="Staircase Dimension Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Staircase Dimension Input: Sales Associate gathers staircase parameters: (a) total floor-to-floor height (vertical rise) in meters; (b) total horizontal run available (floor space for staircase footprint) in meters; (c) staircase width (typical Philippine residential: 0.80m–1.00m); (d) number of flights (straight run, L-shaped with landing, U-shaped with landing); (e) desired step dimensions: target riser height (150–200mm per PD 1096), target tread depth (250–300mm per PD 1096); (f) material preference — treads: plywood (18mm), solid wood (tanguile, narra), tiles on concrete; risers: plywood (12mm), solid wood; stringers: 2×10 or 2×12 lumber; railing: wood (tanguile), steel, aluminum; (g) landing type — none, quarter-turn (L-shape), half-turn (U-shape) with landing dimensions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1050_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1050_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1050_Task6" name="Geometric Calculation &amp; Code Compliance Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Geometric Calculation &amp; Code Compliance Check: System computes staircase geometry: (a) number of risers = total rise ÷ target riser height (rounded up to nearest integer); (b) actual riser height = total rise ÷ number of risers; (c) system validates: riser height ≤ 200mm per PD 1096 (flags non-compliance with warning); (d) number of treads = number of risers − 1 (per flight); (e) total run = number of treads × tread depth; (f) system validates: total run ≤ available horizontal space (flags if insufficient space, recommends shorter tread or L/U configuration); (g) stringer length = √(total rise² + total run²) per flight; (h) for L/U configurations: calculates landing framing dimensions and separate stringer lengths for each flight; (i) system displays 2D side-view diagram of staircase with dimensions
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1050_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1050_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1050_Task7" name="Material Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Quantity Calculation: System generates bill of materials: (a) Treads: quantity = number of treads, width = staircase width, depth = tread depth, material = selected tread material (board footage calculated); (b) Risers: quantity = number of risers, width = staircase width, height = actual riser height, material = selected riser material; (c) Stringers: quantity = 2 (minimum) + 1 intermediate for stairs &gt;1m wide; length per stringer calculated per step 2g; material = 2×10 or 2×12 lumber; (d) Landing framing (if applicable): joists, header beams, plywood decking — per landing dimensions; (e) Railing: newel posts (1 at bottom, 1 at top, 1 at each landing = 2–4 posts), handrail length = stringer length × number of flights, balusters = (handrail length ÷ maximum baluster spacing per PD 1096) − 1 per flight section, baluster height = riser height × number of risers per section + 0.90m (handrail height per code); (f) Hardware: nails, screws, construction adhesive, angle brackets for stringer-to-floor connection; (g) system calculates total board footage and converts to standard lumber lengths available in inventory
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1050_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1050_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1050_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/PDF estimate with: staircase side-view diagram with dimensions, step-by-step code compliance summary, complete bill of materials with quantities, unit prices, and total cost, PD 1096 compliance notes, assembly instructions overview; (b) check inventory availability for all lumber lengths and materials per W533; (c) for non-stock items (special wood species, decorative balusters): create special order per W545; (d) offer home delivery for lumber per W5D; (e) estimate saved to loyalty account and convertible to POS transaction per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1050_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1050_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1050_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1050_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1050_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: provides material quantities only
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1050_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1050_Annotation10" targetRef="W1050_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1050_Flow12" sourceRef="W1050_Start4" targetRef="W1050_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1050_Flow13" sourceRef="W1050_Task5" targetRef="W1050_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1050_Flow14" sourceRef="W1050_Task6" targetRef="W1050_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1050_Flow15" sourceRef="W1050_Task7" targetRef="W1050_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1050_Flow16" sourceRef="W1050_Task8" targetRef="W1050_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1050_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1050_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1050">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1050_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1050_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1050_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1050_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1052" name="W1052. Customer Gutter, Downspout &amp; Flashing Sizing Calculator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests gutter system sizing for new construction, renovation, or replacement
Frequency: ~1,200–1,800 consultations/month across all stores (gutters are part of the lumber &amp; building materials and plumbing categories)
Volume: 1 calculation per customer project
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials/Plumbing Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1052 — Customer Gutter, Downspout &amp; Flashing Sizing Calculator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1052_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1052_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1052_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1052_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1052_Start4" name="Customer requests gutter system sizing for new construction, renovation, or replacement">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1052_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1052_Task5" name="Roof &amp; Building Parameter Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Roof &amp; Building Parameter Input: Sales Associate gathers project parameters: (a) roof type — gable, hip, shed, flat (with parapet), combination; (b) roof dimensions — length and width of each roof plane (or total roof footprint area); (c) roof pitch/slope angle (in degrees or rise-to-run ratio); (d) number of stories (affects downspout length); (e) gutter type preference — half-round (125mm or 150mm), box/K-style (125mm or 150mm), PVC, GI, aluminum; (f) downspout type — round PVC (75mm/100mm), rectangular GI, round GI; (g) building location (for rainfall intensity lookup per PAGASA data per W310); (h) gutter run direction — along eaves (both sides for gable), along all sides (hip roof)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1052_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1052_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1052_Task6" name="Gutter &amp; Downspout Sizing Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Gutter &amp; Downspout Sizing Calculation: System computes hydraulic requirements: (a) roof drainage area per gutter run = roof plane width × horizontal projection (length × cos(pitch)); (b) design rainfall intensity (mm/hr) per PAGASA 10-year return period data for customer&#x27;s location; (c) peak runoff (liters/min) = drainage area (m²) × rainfall intensity (mm/hr) ÷ 60; (d) gutter capacity per profile: half-round 125mm = 1.2 L/s at 1:200 slope, half-round 150mm = 2.0 L/s, box 125mm = 1.5 L/s, box 150mm = 2.5 L/s; (e) if peak runoff exceeds single gutter capacity: system recommends (i) larger profile, (ii) steeper slope, or (iii) additional downspouts to reduce gutter run length; (f) downspout quantity: minimum 1 per 10m of gutter run or 1 per 50m² of drainage area (whichever is greater); (g) downspout length = roof edge height to ground + 300mm extension (splash block or direct to drainage)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1052_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1052_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1052_Task7" name="Flashing &amp; Accessories Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Flashing &amp; Accessories Calculation: System generates complete material list: (a) Gutter sections: total linear meters per gutter profile (standard lengths: 3m or 6m); (b) Gutter brackets/braces: @ 600mm O.C. for PVC, @ 900mm O.C. for GI; (c) End caps: 2 per gutter run (left and right); (d) Joiners/connectors: 1 per section joint; (e) Corner pieces (inside/outside): per roof plan corners; (f) Downspout sections: total length per downspout × number of downspouts (standard lengths: 3m); (g) Downspout elbows: 2 per downspout (top offset from gutter, bottom offset away from wall); (h) Downspout brackets/wall clips: @ 1.5m O.C.; (i) Splash blocks or flexible downspout extensions: 1 per downspout; (j) Valley flashing: length × number of valleys (for gable/hip intersections); (k) Apron flashing: at roof-wall intersections; (l) Step flashing: at chimney/penetration interfaces; (m) Sealant and pop rivets/screws for assembly; (n) Leaf guard/screen: optional, same linear meters as gutter
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1052_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1052_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1052_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/PDF estimate with: roof drainage diagram, hydraulic calculation summary, recommended gutter profile and downspout configuration, complete bill of materials with quantities and prices, total estimated project cost, installation instructions overview; (b) check inventory per W533; (c) for non-stock items (special gutter profiles, aluminum flashing): special order per W545; (d) offer delivery per W5D for long gutter sections; (e) offer contractor referral per W904; (f) estimate saved and convertible to sale per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1052_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1052_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1052_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1052_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1052_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1052_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1052_Annotation10" targetRef="W1052_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1052_Flow12" sourceRef="W1052_Start4" targetRef="W1052_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1052_Flow13" sourceRef="W1052_Task5" targetRef="W1052_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1052_Flow14" sourceRef="W1052_Task6" targetRef="W1052_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1052_Flow15" sourceRef="W1052_Task7" targetRef="W1052_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1052_Flow16" sourceRef="W1052_Task8" targetRef="W1052_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1052_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1052_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1052">
