    <bpmn:process id="W_W1053" name="W1053. Customer Bathroom &amp; Kitchen Exhaust Fan &amp; Ventilation Duct Sizing Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests exhaust fan recommendation for bathroom, kitchen, or other ventilation application
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 consultations/month across all stores (home appliances category: 5% of SKUs, ~1,750 items; exhaust fans are a high-turn sub-category)
Volume: 1 sizing calculation per room
Owner: Home Appliances Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Appliances Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1053 — Customer Bathroom &amp; Kitchen Exhaust Fan &amp; Ventilation Duct Sizing Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1053_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1053_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1053_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1053_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1053_Start4" name="Customer requests exhaust fan recommendation for bathroom, kitchen, or other ventilation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1053_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1053_Task5" name="Room Parameter Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Room Parameter Input: Sales Associate gathers room details: (a) application — bathroom, kitchen, laundry, workshop, storage room; (b) room dimensions — length, width, height (in meters); (c) room volume = length × width × height (m³); (d) existing duct/vent opening — yes/no, diameter if existing; (e) wall type — CHB (concrete hollow block, requires core drilling for new opening), wood frame, drywall; (f) ceiling type — suspended ceiling (space for inline fan above), solid concrete slab (wall-mount fan only); (g) power source — wall outlet available, or hardwired connection needed; (h) special features — humidity sensor, timer, backdraft damper, speed control
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Home Appliances Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1053_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1053_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1053_Task6" name="CMH Requirement &amp; Fan Sizing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CMH Requirement &amp; Fan Sizing: System calculates required airflow: (a) minimum CMH = room volume × target ACH (bathroom: 8–10, kitchen: 15–20, laundry: 5–8, workshop: 6–10); (b) system recommends fan models from inventory with rated CMH ≥ minimum CMH; (c) system selects recommended duct size: 4&quot; (100mm) for CMH ≤200, 5&quot; (125mm) for CMH 200–400, 6&quot; (150mm) for CMH 400–800; (d) for kitchen range hoods: additional consideration — hood width ≥ cooktop width, mounting height 600–750mm above cooktop, duct run to exterior (maximum 3m with 1 elbow, or upgrade to higher CMH for longer runs); (e) system shows top 3 fan model recommendations with: brand, model, rated CMH, duct diameter, noise level (sones), power consumption (watts), price
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1053_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1053_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1053_Task7" name="Duct &amp; Accessories Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Duct &amp; Accessories Specification: System generates complete material list: (a) exhaust fan unit (recommended model); (b) ducting — rigid aluminum duct (preferred) or flexible aluminum duct, diameter per step 2, length = distance from fan to exterior wall/roof vent + 0.5m contingency; (c) exterior wall vent/roof cap with backdraft damper (prevents outside air entry when fan is off); (d) duct tape or clamps for connections; (e) wall/ceiling mounting hardware; (f) exterior louver/grille (aesthetic cover); (g) for new wall penetration in CHB: core drilling service recommendation per W138 (installation services) — typical cost PHP 500–1,500 per hole; (h) optional upgrades: speed controller, humidity sensor, timer switch
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1053_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1053_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1053_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates estimate with: room ventilation calculation (volume, ACH, CMH), recommended fan with specifications, complete duct and accessory list, total cost, estimated installation time (DIY: 1–3 hours, professional: 1–2 hours); (b) offer installation service booking per W138; (c) estimate saved and convertible per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Home Appliances Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1053_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1053_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1053_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1053_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1053_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Home Appliances Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1053_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1053_Annotation10" targetRef="W1053_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
