    <bpmn:process id="W_W1055" name="W1055. Customer Water Filtration &amp; Purification System Sizing for Residential &amp; Commercial" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests water filtration/purification system recommendation for residential or commercial application
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 consultations/month across all stores (plumbing category: 12% of SKUs; water filtration is a growing sub-category driven by Philippine water quality concerns)
Volume: 1 system sizing per consultation
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1055 — Customer Water Filtration &amp; Purification System Sizing for Residential &amp; Commercial</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1055_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1055_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1055_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1055_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1055_Start4" name="Customer requests water filtration/purification system recommendation for residential or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1055_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1055_Task5" name="Water Quality &amp; Usage Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Water Quality &amp; Usage Assessment: Sales Associate gathers water source and usage information: (a) water source — municipal/city water district, deep well, shallow well, rainwater, community water system; (b) known water quality issues — sediment/cloudiness, chlorine taste/smell, hardness (scale buildup on fixtures), staining (iron/manganese — brown/orange), TDS (total dissolved solids — if customer has TDS meter reading), bacterial contamination (if known); (c) household size — number of persons (determines daily water demand); (d) filtration points — point-of-use (under-sink for drinking/cooking only), point-of-entry (whole-house for all taps); (e) installation location — under kitchen sink, outside house, garage/utility room; (f) budget range; (g) if customer is uncertain about water quality, recommend water testing kit (BuildRight stocks DIY test kits for pH, TDS, hardness, iron) or local water testing laboratory referral
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1055_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1055_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1055_Task6" name="System Type Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System Type Recommendation: System recommends filtration stages based on water quality assessment: (a) Municipal water (typical quality): 3-stage under-sink system — (1) 5-micron sediment filter → (2) granular activated carbon (GAC) filter → (3) 1-micron carbon block filter; adequate for most Manila Water/Maynilad supplied areas; (b) Municipal water with intermittent supply (pressure fluctuations cause pipe contamination): 3-stage + UV sterilizer — add UV lamp (typically 11W or 24W depending on flow rate) after carbon filtration; (c) Well water (high TDS, possible contamination): 5-stage RO system — (1) sediment → (2) carbon → (3) carbon block → (4) RO membrane (50–100 GPD) → (5) post-carbon polishing filter; plus UV for bacterial safety; (d) Hard water (scale buildup): water softener before filtration — ion exchange resin tank sized to household daily consumption and grain hardness; (e) Whole-house system: point-of-entry (POE) — larger filter housings (20&quot; big blue) with sediment + carbon stages, sized to household peak flow rate (typical: 15–30 liters/min for 3–5 person household)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1055_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1055_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1055_Task7" name="Component Specification &amp; Sizing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Component Specification &amp; Sizing: System generates bill of materials for recommended system: (a) filter housings — number of stages × housing size (10&quot; standard for under-sink, 20&quot; big blue for POE); (b) filter cartridges per stage — type, micron rating, replacement interval (sediment: 3–6 months, carbon: 6–12 months, RO membrane: 2–3 years); (c) UV sterilizer unit — wattage (11W for under-sink, 24W–40W for whole-house), replacement lamp interval: 12 months; (d) RO system components — booster pump (if inlet pressure &lt;40 PSI), storage tank (3.2G or 10G), faucet; (e) water softener — resin tank size (1 cu.ft. for typical household), brine tank, control valve; (f) pipework and fittings — 1/4&quot; tubing for under-sink RO, 1/2&quot; or 3/4&quot; pipe for POE; (g) installation accessories — mounting bracket, ball valves (inlet/outlet isolation), pressure gauge, TDS meter (for RO systems); (h) system calculates total cost and annual maintenance cost (replacement cartridges and UV lamp)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1055_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1055_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1055_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates estimate with: water quality assessment summary, recommended system diagram, bill of materials, total cost, annual maintenance schedule with replacement costs, estimated filter life based on household consumption; (b) offer installation service per W138; (c) offer annual filter replacement subscription reminder (SMS notification when filter replacement is due based on purchase date + estimated life); (d) estimate saved per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1055_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1055_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1055_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1055_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1055_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: purchase for &gt;PHP 5,000 systems; operational: should send proactive replacement reminders
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1055_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1055_Annotation10" targetRef="W1055_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1055_Flow12" sourceRef="W1055_Start4" targetRef="W1055_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1055_Flow13" sourceRef="W1055_Task5" targetRef="W1055_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1055_Flow14" sourceRef="W1055_Task6" targetRef="W1055_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1055_Flow15" sourceRef="W1055_Task7" targetRef="W1055_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1055_Flow16" sourceRef="W1055_Task8" targetRef="W1055_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
