    <bpmn:process id="W_W1056" name="W1056. Store-Level Customer Construction Permit Advisory &amp; Municipal Building Requirements Guidance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer asks about construction permit requirements during building materials consultation
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 advisory interactions/month across all stores
Volume: 1 advisory session per customer (often in conjunction with a materials estimation service)
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1056 — Store-Level Customer Construction Permit Advisory &amp; Municipal Building Requirements Guidance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1056_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1056_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1056_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1056_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1056_Start4" name="Customer asks about construction permit requirements during building materials…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1056_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1056_Task5" name="Project Classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Classification: Sales Associate identifies the customer&#x27;s project type: (a) new residential construction (single-family, 1–3 stories); (b) residential renovation/remodel (interior, exterior, extension/addition); (c) small commercial construction (store, warehouse, workshop); (d) fence/wall construction; (e) swimming pool; (f) solar panel installation; (g) electrical upgrade (panel replacement, additional circuits); (h) plumbing modification (new bathroom, septic tank); (i) other. System displays the general permit requirements for the identified project type based on the customer&#x27;s LGU jurisdiction (per W310 address hierarchy and LGU database)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1056_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1056_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1056_Task6" name="Permit Requirements Information Guide">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Permit Requirements Information Guide: System generates a printable permit requirements guide for the customer&#x27;s project type and LGU: (a) New Residential Construction: (i) Building Permit: signed and sealed plans by licensed architect and structural engineer, barangay clearance, tax declaration, vicinity map, fire safety plan (for ≥2 stories); (ii) Electrical Permit: electrical plan signed by licensed Professional Electrical Engineer (PEE); (iii) Plumbing Permit: plumbing plan signed by licensed Master Plumber; (iv) Zoning Clearance; (v) BFP FSIC (for ≥2 stories or commercial); (vi) typical permit processing time: 10–30 business days per LGU; (vii) typical permit cost: 0.5–1% of estimated construction cost; (b) Renovation/Remodel: (i) Building Permit may or may not be required depending on scope — structural changes, additional floor, or change of occupancy always require permit; cosmetic changes (painting, flooring, cabinets) typically do not; (ii) Electrical/Plumbing permits for any modification to existing systems; (c) Fence/Wall: (i) Building Permit typically required for fences &gt;1.80m height per PD 1096; (ii) Barangay clearance; (d) Solar Installation: (i) Electrical Permit from LGU; (ii) Net-Metering application with local distribution utility (DU/EC); (iii) structural clearance if roof-mounted (additional dead load and wind load); (e) Common LGU-Specific Additions: (i) Cebu City: Additional Green Building compliance per local ordinance; (ii) Davao City: Rainwater collection system per Davao City ordinance; (iii) Quezon City: Green Building Code compliance for ≥10,000 sqm; (iv) system notes: &quot;Requirements shown are general guidance only. Contact your LGU Office of the Building Official (OBO) for the specific and current requirements for your project&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated generation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1056_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1056_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1056_Task7" name="Professional Referral &amp; Guidance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Professional Referral &amp; Guidance: (a) system provides referral list for professional services: (i) Licensed architects and civil engineers (from BuildRight&#x27;s contractor referral database per W904); (ii) Licensed electricians and plumbers; (iii) BFP-accredited fire safety service providers (for fire safety plans); (b) system prints &quot;Next Steps&quot; checklist: (i) Contact LGU OBO for current requirements and fees; (ii) Engage licensed architect/engineer for plans and specifications; (iii) Obtain barangay clearance; (iv) Submit permit application; (v) Upon permit approval, return to BuildRight for materials quotation per W542 or W162; (c) system offers to save the requirements guide to customer&#x27;s loyalty account for future reference
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1056_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1056_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1056_Task8" name="Materials Estimation Integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Materials Estimation Integration: (a) if customer has their building plan and material specifications, Sales Associate can proceed to materials estimation services: W1044 (concrete calculator), W1043 (paint calculator), W1050 (staircase calculator), W983 (roofing calculator), W989 (plumbing layout), W991 (electrical circuit design); (b) if customer has a contractor, offer to send the requirements guide to their contractor via email/SMS for coordination; (c) if customer&#x27;s project is a B2B trade/corporate account, refer to pro desk per W112 for full project quotation per W162
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–5 min (optional continuation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1056_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1056_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1056_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1056_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1056_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: cannot guarantee accuracy for every LGU
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1056_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1056_Annotation10" targetRef="W1056_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1056_Flow12" sourceRef="W1056_Start4" targetRef="W1056_Task5" />
