    <bpmn:process id="W_W1057" name="W1057. Customer Insulation Material Calculator (Wall, Ceiling, Roof Thermal &amp; Acoustic)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests insulation quantity estimate for residential or small commercial building project
Frequency: ~600–1,000 consultations/month across all stores (insulation is a growing category driven by Philippine energy efficiency awareness and Green Building Code adoption)
Volume: 1 calculation per project
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1057 — Customer Insulation Material Calculator (Wall, Ceiling, Roof Thermal &amp; Acoustic)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1057_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1057_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1057_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1057_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1057_Start4" name="Customer requests insulation quantity estimate for residential or small commercial…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1057_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1057_Task5" name="Application &amp; Climate Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Application &amp; Climate Assessment: Sales Associate gathers project parameters: (a) insulation application — exterior wall, interior partition wall, ceiling (below attic), attic floor, roof (under-roof/above-ceiling), floor (above crawl space), acoustic partition; (b) building type — single-family detached, townhouse/rowhouse (shared wall), condominium, commercial; (c) air-conditioned spaces — yes/no (determines thermal insulation value); (d) climate zone — based on customer&#x27;s location per W310 (Philippine climate zones: Type I — two pronounced seasons, Type II — no dry season, Type III — dry season short, Type IV — rainfall evenly distributed); (e) objective — thermal (reduce cooling cost), acoustic (noise reduction), both thermal and acoustic, fire-rated (compartmentalization); (f) wall construction — CHB (hollow block) with furring, wood frame, steel frame, concrete solid; (g) available cavity depth — determines maximum insulation thickness
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1057_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1057_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1057_Task6" name="R-Value &amp; Material Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: R-Value &amp; Material Recommendation: System recommends insulation material and thickness: (a) Thermal — exterior wall: recommended R-value R-13 to R-19 for Philippine climate (lower than temperate countries due to smaller indoor-outdoor temperature differential); fiberglass batt R-13 (89mm) or R-19 (152mm) for framed walls; rigid foam board 50mm–75mm for CHB furred walls; (b) Thermal — ceiling/roof (most impactful application in Philippines): recommended R-30 (241mm fiberglass) or equivalent in rigid board + radiant barrier for attic/roof applications; radiant barrier alone reduces radiant heat gain by 25–40% in Philippine metal roof installations; (c) Acoustic — interior partition: rock wool 50mm (STC 45–50) or fiberglass batt 89mm (STC 38–43) with resilient channel; (d) Fire-rated partition: rock wool 50mm–100mm (fire rating 1–2 hours) per BFP requirement per W476; (e) system recommends material based on: application, available cavity depth, objective (thermal/acoustic/fire), and budget
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1057_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1057_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1057_Task7" name="Area &amp; Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Area &amp; Quantity Calculation: System calculates insulation quantities: (a) total wall/ceiling/roof area = length × height (for walls) or length × width (for ceilings/roofs), minus deductions (windows, doors, openings); (b) for batt/blanket insulation: number of rolls = total area ÷ coverage per roll (product-specific, e.g., 11.6 m² per roll for 400mm × 6m batt), rounded up; (c) for rigid board insulation: number of boards = total area ÷ area per board (standard: 1.2m × 2.4m = 2.88 m² per board), rounded up; (d) for radiant barrier (roof): linear meters = roof ridge length × 1.15 (waste factor for overlapping joints), width per roll (typically 1.2m or 1.5m); (e) companion materials: (i) vapor barrier (polyethylene sheeting, 0.15mm, for warm-humid climate — install on exterior side of insulation), (ii) insulation supports/wire rods (for ceiling applications, @ 600mm O.C.), (iii) reflective tape for radiant barrier joints, (iv) sealant/caulk for gap sealing, (v) protective equipment: gloves, long-sleeve shirt, dust mask (for fiberglass per W172 PPE requirements)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1057_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1057_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1057_Task8" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates estimate with: application summary, recommended R-value and material, area calculation, complete bill of materials, total cost, energy savings estimate (for thermal applications: &quot;Estimated cooling cost reduction: 20–30% for ceiling insulation, 10–15% for wall insulation&quot;), installation overview; (b) check inventory per W533; (c) offer installation referral per W138/W904; (d) estimate saved per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1057_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1057_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1057_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1057_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1057_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must display fire safety warning
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1057_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1057_Annotation10" targetRef="W1057_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1057_Flow12" sourceRef="W1057_Start4" targetRef="W1057_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1057_Flow13" sourceRef="W1057_Task5" targetRef="W1057_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1057_Flow14" sourceRef="W1057_Task6" targetRef="W1057_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1057_Flow15" sourceRef="W1057_Task7" targetRef="W1057_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1057_Flow16" sourceRef="W1057_Task8" targetRef="W1057_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1057_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1057_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1057">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1057_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1057_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1057_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1057_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1060" name="W1060. Customer Rebar Stirrup, Tying Wire &amp; Binding Material Quantity Estimator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests rebar accessory quantities (stirrups, tying wire, spacers) for a reinforced concrete project
Frequency: ~2,500–3,500 consultations/month across all stores (rebar and reinforcing accessories are core items in the lumber &amp; building materials category — 14% of SKUs)
Volume: 1 estimation per project
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1060 — Customer Rebar Stirrup, Tying Wire &amp; Binding Material Quantity Estimator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1060_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1060_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1060_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1060_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1060_Start4" name="Customer requests rebar accessory quantities (stirrups, tying wire, spacers) for a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1060_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1060_Task5" name="Structural Element &amp; Rebar Configuration Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Structural Element &amp; Rebar Configuration Input: Sales Associate gathers project parameters: (a) structural element type — column, beam, slab, footing, retaining wall; (b) element dimensions — (i) column: width × depth × height; (ii) beam: width × depth × length; (iii) slab: length × width × thickness; (iv) footing: length × width × depth; (c) longitudinal rebar — diameter (10mm, 12mm, 16mm, 20mm, 25mm) and number of bars per element (typical: 4–8 bars per column, 4–6 bars per beam); (d) stirrup/tie bar diameter (typically 10mm for columns, 8–10mm for beams); (e) stirrup spacing per engineer&#x27;s specification (typical: 100mm at ends/ joints, 200mm at midspan — or uniform 150mm for simple residential); (f) concrete cover (typical: 40mm interior, 50mm exterior); (g) if customer has structural plan: system accepts direct input of bar schedule (diameter, number, length, bending schedule) — provides the most accurate estimation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1060_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1060_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1060_Task6" name="Stirrup Quantity &amp; Cutting Schedule Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Stirrup Quantity &amp; Cutting Schedule Calculation: System computes stirrup requirements: (a) stirrup perimeter per piece: for rectangular column/beam stirrup = 2 × (width − 2 × cover) + 2 × (depth − 2 × cover) + hook length (typically 75mm × 2 hooks); (b) stirrup length per piece = perimeter (including hooks); (c) number of stirrups = element length ÷ stirrup spacing + 1 (first stirrup at 50mm from end); (d) total stirrup bar length = number of stirrups × length per piece; (e) system converts to number of 6m standard bars: total stirrup bar length ÷ 6m, rounded up; (f) system generates cutting schedule for in-store rebar cutting/bending per W986: piece number, stirrup dimensions (inside width × inside depth), bend angle (90° × 4 corners), hook length, quantity; (g) for circular columns: stirrup perimeter = π × (diameter − 2 × cover) + overlap (typically 300mm for lap splice)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1060_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1060_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1060_Task7" name="Tying Wire, Spacer &amp; Accessory Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Tying Wire, Spacer &amp; Accessory Calculation: System computes accessory quantities: (a) Tying wire: (i) total rebar weight (longitudinal bars + stirrups) = number of bars × length × weight per meter (per diameter); (ii) tying wire quantity = total rebar weight × 0.015 (1.5 kg wire per 100 kg rebar); (iii) sold in 1 kg coils — round up to nearest coil; (b) Concrete spacers: (i) for columns: 4 spacers per stirrup × number of stirrups (to maintain cover on each face); (ii) for beams: 2–4 spacers per stirrup; (iii) for slabs: 1 spacer per m² (distributed on chairs/supports); (iv) sold in bags of 50; (c) Rebar chairs/supports (for slab reinforcement): 1 per m² of slab area at the bottom mat; (d) Mechanical couplers (if specified by engineer): per bar splice schedule, each coupler replaces 1 lap splice; (e) Rebar caps (safety — cover exposed rebar ends per OSHA/DOLE safety per W140): 1 per exposed bar end
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1060_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1060_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1060_Task8" name="Estimate Generation, Cutting/Bending &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate Generation, Cutting/Bending &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates comprehensive estimate with: structural element summary, longitudinal rebar schedule (diameter, number, length, weight, cost), stirrup cutting schedule (per piece dimensions, number of pieces, 6m bar consumption, cost), tying wire quantity (kg, cost), spacers and accessories (quantity, cost), total project cost; (b) if customer requests in-store rebar cutting/bending for stirrups: system sends cutting schedule to W986 (rebar cutting &amp; bending service) for execution; (c) for large orders (&gt;500 kg rebar): offer site delivery per W964 (bulk delivery); (d) for trade/corporate accounts: convert to project quote per W162; (e) estimate saved per W542
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1060_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1060_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1060_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1060_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1060_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must display disclaimer: &quot;Rebar quantities shown are based on customer-provided specifications. BuildRight does not provide structural engineering services. Consult a licensed civil engineer for proper rebar design per NSCP (National Structural Code of the Philippines).&quot;
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1060_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1060_Annotation10" targetRef="W1060_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
