    <bpmn:process id="W_W1061" name="W1061. Customer Tile Grout, Adhesive &amp; Thin-Set Mortar Quantity Calculator Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases tiles or requests tile installation material quantities
Frequency: ~4,000–6,000 consultations/month across all stores (tiles &amp; flooring: 12% of SKUs, ~4,200 items — this is the natural companion service to W963 tile quantity calculator)
Volume: 1 calculation per tiling project
Owner: Tiles &amp; Flooring Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Tiles Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1061 — Customer Tile Grout, Adhesive &amp; Thin-Set Mortar Quantity Calculator Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1061_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1061_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1061_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1061_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1061_Start4" name="Customer purchases tiles or requests tile installation material quantities">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1061_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1061_Task5" name="Project Parameter Input (Integration with W963)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Parameter Input (Integration with W963): Sales Associate gathers tiling project parameters (or pulls from W963 estimate if already completed): (a) tile type — ceramic, porcelain, natural stone (granite, marble, travertine), mosaic, vinyl tile; (b) tile dimensions — length × width × thickness (mm); (c) total tiled area (m²) from W963 or manual input; (d) application — floor, wall, countertop, backsplash, shower/tub surround (wet area), outdoor; (e) substrate — concrete slab, cement screed, existing tile (re-tiling), plywood, gypsum board (wall tile only); (f) joint width — 2mm (min. for rectified tiles), 3mm (standard for ceramic/porcelain), 5–10mm (for rustic/natural stone); (g) grout type preference — cementitious (standard), epoxy (wet areas/chemical resistance), urethane (stain resistant); (h) adhesive type — pre-mixed mastic (wall tile, dry areas only), standard thin-set mortar (dry-mix, cement-based), modified thin-set (polymer-modified, for porcelain and wet areas), epoxy adhesive (for chemical-resistant/industrial)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Tiles &amp; Flooring Dept Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1061_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1061_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1061_Task6" name="Adhesive/Thin-Set Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Adhesive/Thin-Set Quantity Calculation: System computes adhesive quantity: (a) trowel notch size recommended per tile type: (i) tiles ≤100mm × 100mm (mosaic): 6mm V-notch; (ii) tiles 100–300mm: 8mm square-notch; (iii) tiles 300–600mm: 10mm square-notch; (iv) tiles &gt;600mm or natural stone: 12mm square-notch; (b) adhesive coverage rate per trowel notch: 6mm = ~5 m² per 20kg bag; 8mm = ~4 m² per 20kg bag; 10mm = ~3 m² per 20kg bag; 12mm = ~2.5 m² per 20kg bag; (c) adjust for substrate condition: rough/unflat substrate: ×1.3 (additional material to compensate for unevenness); smooth/flat substrate: ×1.0; (d) total adhesive bags = total area ÷ coverage rate × substrate factor, rounded up; (e) for wet areas (shower surround, bathroom floor): add waterproofing membrane quantity = area ÷ coverage per roll (typically 10 m² per 20kg pail of liquid membrane, or 15 m² per roll of sheet membrane)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1061_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1061_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1061_Task7" name="Grout Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Grout Quantity Calculation: System computes grout quantity: (a) grout volume formula per linear meter of joint: joint depth (mm) × joint width (mm) × 1m ÷ 1,000,000 = m³ per linear meter; (b) joint depth = tile thickness (full depth for full-bed installation; or 2/3 of tile thickness for thin-bed); (c) total joint length (linear meters): (i) for rectangular tiles: total area ÷ tile length + total area ÷ tile width = approximate total joint length; (ii) system adds perimeter joint length (perimeter of tiled area — expansion joint); (d) total grout volume = total joint length × grout volume per linear meter; (e) grout density: cementitious grout ≈ 1,600 kg/m³ (1.6 kg/L); epoxy grout ≈ 1,800 kg/m³ (1.8 kg/L); (f) total grout weight (kg) = total grout volume × density; (g) bags of grout = total weight ÷ bag size (1kg, 2kg, or 5kg), rounded up; (h) for epoxy grout: system calculates Part A (resin) and Part B (hardener) units
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1061_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1061_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1061_Task8" name="Complete Installation Material List &amp; Estimate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Complete Installation Material List &amp; Estimate: System generates full bill of materials: (a) Adhesive/thin-set: type, number of bags, price; (b) Grout: type, color options, number of bags/units, price; (c) Tile spacers: 1 bag per 5 m² (bag of 200 pieces); size matches joint width (2mm, 3mm, 5mm); (d) Waterproofing membrane (if wet area): type, quantity, price; (e) Primer (if needed for modified thin-set on non-porous substrate): 1 liter per 4 m²; (f) Notched trowel: 1 per project (size per step 2a); (g) Grout float: 1 per project; (h) Sponge and bucket: 1 per project (for grout cleanup); (i) Tile cutter rental: per W139 (tool rental) or purchase; (j) Rubber mallet: 1 per project (for tapping tiles level); (k) Level (600mm or 1200mm): 1 per project; (l) Crack isolation membrane (optional): for substrates with existing cracks; (m) system calculates total project cost including all materials; (n) system generates estimate per W542 with optional installation referral per W138/W904
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Tiles &amp; Flooring Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1061_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1061_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1061_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1061_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1061_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Tiles &amp; Flooring Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1061_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1061_Annotation10" targetRef="W1061_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1061_Flow12" sourceRef="W1061_Start4" targetRef="W1061_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1061_Flow13" sourceRef="W1061_Task5" targetRef="W1061_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1061_Flow14" sourceRef="W1061_Task6" targetRef="W1061_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1061_Flow15" sourceRef="W1061_Task7" targetRef="W1061_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1061_Flow16" sourceRef="W1061_Task8" targetRef="W1061_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1061_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1061_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1061">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1061_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1061_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1061_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1061_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1064" name="W1064. Customer Electrical Panel &amp; Circuit Breaker Sizing Recommendation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests electrical panel sizing, circuit breaker selection, or load center configuration for residential or small commercial construction project
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 customer interactions/month across all stores (electrical is 10% of SKUs, ~3,500 items)
Volume: 1 panel/load center design per customer visit
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1064 — Customer Electrical Panel &amp; Circuit Breaker Sizing Recommendation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1064_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1064_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1064_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1064_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1064_Start4" name="Customer requests electrical panel sizing, circuit breaker selection, or load center…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1064_Task5" name="Project Load Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Load Assessment: Sales Associate gathers electrical project details: (a) project type — new residential construction, renovation/addition, small commercial (sari-sari store, bakery, workshop), or appliance upgrade; (b) total floor area (sqm) and number of floors; (c) major electrical loads: air conditioning units (count, type: window/split, HP/BTU rating), electric water heater (yes/no, kW), electric stove/cooker (yes/no, kW), refrigerator, washing machine, microwave, pump motor (HP); (d) lighting load: LED (wattage per room, room count); (e) convenience outlet count by room; (f) special loads: elevator, pool pump, workshop equipment, EV charger; (g) service entrance: MERALCO / Davao Light / local electric cooperative, single-phase or three-phase supply available
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1064_Task6" name="Total Connected Load &amp; Demand Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Total Connected Load &amp; Demand Calculation: System computes electrical load per PEC 2017: (a) general lighting load = total floor area × 36 VA/sqm (PEC Table); (b) small appliance branch circuits = minimum two 20A circuits at 1,500 VA each; (c) laundry circuit = 1,500 VA; (d) individual appliance loads per nameplate ratings; (e) largest motor load (typically aircon compressor) × 125% per PEC; (f) demand factor applied per PEC Table (first 3,000 VA at 100%, next 117,000 VA at 35%, remainder at 25% for residential); (g) system outputs: total connected load (VA), estimated demand load (VA after demand factors), recommended service rating (100A, 150A, 200A, or higher), recommended service entrance wire size (AWG) per W982
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1064_Task7" name="Panel Board &amp; Circuit Breaker Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Panel Board &amp; Circuit Breaker Configuration: System designs panel layout: (a) selects main circuit breaker (MCB) rating matching service rating (100A/150A/200A); (b) allocates branch circuits: lighting circuits (15A each, max 10 outlets per circuit per PEC), convenience outlet circuits (20A each, max 6 outlets per circuit), dedicated circuits for major appliances (aircon: 30A/40A per unit, water heater: 30A/40A, electric stove: 50A/60A, pump: 20A/30A); (c) selects wire size per circuit per PEC Table (14 AWG for 15A, 12 AWG for 20A, 10 AWG for 30A, 8 AWG for 40A, 6 AWG for 50A/60A); (d) specifies safety devices: ELCB/GFCI (30mA trip) for wet areas (bathroom, kitchen, outdoor), SPD for main panel, automatic voltage regulator (AVR) recommendation for areas with unstable power; (e) system generates panel schedule diagram showing circuit number, breaker rating, wire size, load description, and phase assignment (for three-phase: balance loads across phases within 10% imbalance tolerance per PEC)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1064_Task8" name="Complete Material List &amp; Bill of Quantities">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Complete Material List &amp; Bill of Quantities: System generates full BOM: (a) panel board enclosure (surface-mount or flush-mount, indoor/outdoor rated, IP rating for outdoor); (b) main breaker and branch breakers by brand carried in inventory (Schneider/Merte, ABB, GE, Siemens, Panasonic/Fujihoki — major brands available in PH); (c) ELCB/RCD devices; (d) SPD; (e) wire/cable per circuit (length estimated from floor area × 1.5 factor for routing per W982); (f) electrical metallic tubing (EMT) or PVC conduit per circuit; (g) junction boxes, outlet boxes, switch boxes; (h) switches (1-gang, 2-gang, 3-gang) and convenience outlets (with grounding per PEC); (i) panel board accessories: neutral bar, ground bar, panel cover, circuit directory label; (j) electrical tape, wire nuts, cable ties; (k) estimated total material cost; (l) for trade accounts, system applies contracted pricing per W163
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1064_Task9" name="Estimate Generation, Safety Advisory &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Estimate Generation, Safety Advisory &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) system generates printable/PDF estimate with: load calculation summary, panel schedule diagram, complete BOM with quantities and prices, total estimated cost; (b) safety advisory printed on estimate: &quot;Electrical installations must comply with the Philippine Electrical Code (PEC) 2017. All work should be performed by a licensed Professional Electrical Engineer (PEE) or Registered Master Electrician (RME). This material list is for quantity estimation only and does not substitute for professional electrical design. BuildRight Depot recommends engaging a licensed electrician for installation.&quot;; (c) for B2B/trade customers, estimate converts to project quote per W162; (d) system offers optional: list of licensed electrician partners in customer&#x27;s area per W904 (contractor referral service); (e) estimate saved to customer loyalty account per W17
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1064_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1064_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1064_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1064_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must enforce brand consistency within a single panel configuration; operational: should recommend AVR and SPD for these areas based on store location
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1064_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1064_Annotation11" targetRef="W1064_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
