    <bpmn:process id="W_W1083" name="W1083. Store-Level Customer Plumbing Fixture &amp; Fitting Compatibility Verification Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer brings a plumbing fixture, fitting, valve, or pipe sample to the store for matching, or requests help designing a plumbing layout for a residential or small commercial project
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 customer interactions/month across all stores (plumbing is 12% of SKUs, ~4,200 items)
Volume: 1–5 fixture compatibility checks per customer visit
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1083 — Store-Level Customer Plumbing Fixture &amp; Fitting Compatibility Verification Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1083_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1083_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1083_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1083_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1083_Start4" name="Customer brings a plumbing fixture, fitting, valve, or pipe sample to the store for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1083_Task5" name="Customer Project &amp; Fixture Context Gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Project &amp; Fixture Context Gathering: Sales Associate identifies the customer&#x27;s need: (a) replacement part matching — customer brings existing fixture/fitting for replacement; (b) new installation — customer is building or renovating and needs a complete plumbing fixture set; (c) repair — customer has a leak or break and needs the correct repair part; (d) upgrade — customer wants to replace an older fixture with a modern equivalent. Associate records: fixture location (bathroom, kitchen, laundry, outdoor), fixture type (faucet, valve, drain, toilet, shower head, water heater connection), existing pipe material visible at installation point (GI, PPR, PVC, copper, PE), and approximate pipe diameter if known
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1083_Task6" name="Physical Sample Inspection &amp; Thread/Material Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Physical Sample Inspection &amp; Thread/Material Identification: For customers bringing samples: (a) Associate measures thread diameter using a thread pitch gauge (BSP threads have ½&quot; BSP ≈ 21mm OD, ¾&quot; BSP ≈ 26.5mm OD, 1&quot; BSP ≈ 33.3mm OD); (b) identifies thread type: male vs. female, tapered (BSPT) vs. parallel (BSPP); (c) identifies material: GI (silver-gray, magnetic), brass (gold/yellow, non-magnetic), PPR (green or white plastic), PVC (white or gray plastic, lighter than PPR), copper (reddish-brown), PE (black flexible tubing); (d) checks seal type required: Teflon tape, pipe sealant (locktite), rubber gasket, O-ring, or solvent cement; (e) for faucets: identifies mounting type (wall-mount, deck-mount, single-hole, centerset, widespread), handle configuration (single-lever, dual-handle), and cartridge type (ceramic disc, compression, ball); (f) for drains: measures drain hole diameter (standard Philippine wash basin: 1¼&quot; or 1½&quot;), checks overflow presence/absence, identifies trap type (P-trap, S-trap, bottle trap)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1083_Task7" name="System-Assisted Compatibility Lookup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System-Assisted Compatibility Lookup: System performs compatibility matching: (a) system matches the identified thread type, size, and material against compatible products in inventory; (b) cross-reference table maintained in product attribute master (W298) links every faucet model to compatible valves, supply hoses, drain assemblies, and mounting hardware; (c) system flags incompatibilities: e.g., &quot;Selected faucet requires ½&quot; BSP female inlet. Customer&#x27;s existing supply line is ⅜&quot; compression. Adapter fitting needed: ⅜&quot; compression × ½&quot; BSP male (SKU #XXXX)&quot;; (d) system recommends transition fittings for cross-material joins: GI-to-PPR transition union, PVC-to-GI threaded adapter, PPR-to-copper compression fitting; (e) for toilets: system verifies rough-in distance (standard Philippine: 12&quot; or 10&quot; from wall to closet flange center), bowl shape (round vs. elongated), flush type (gravity, pressure-assisted, dual-flush), and water supply connection type; (f) system displays compatibility status for each selected item: ✓ Compatible, ⚠ Adapter Required (with specific SKU), ✗ Not Compatible (with alternative recommendation)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1083_Task8" name="Complete Fixture Set Assembly &amp; Companion Products">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Complete Fixture Set Assembly &amp; Companion Products: System generates a complete fixture package with all required accessories: (a) for a faucet installation: faucet body + supply hoses (hot/cold, correct length) + angle stop valves (matching pipe type) + Teflon tape + mounting hardware + escutcheon/deck plate; (b) for a toilet installation: toilet bowl + tank + closet flange + wax ring/sponge gasket + toilet bolts + supply valve + flexible supply hose + toilet seat cover; (c) for a shower installation: shower valve (concealed vs. exposed) + shower head + arm + diverter (if combined with tub spout) + hot/cold supply connections + rough-in valve body; (d) recommended tools: adjustable wrench, basin wrench, pipe cutter (for material type), Teflon tape, plumber&#x27;s putty, silicone sealant; (e) for trade account customers, system applies contracted pricing per W163 and offers bulk quantity breaks
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1083_Task9" name="Estimate Generation &amp; Installation Advisory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Estimate Generation &amp; Installation Advisory: (a) system generates itemized estimate with compatibility notes for each item; (b) installation advisory printed on estimate: &quot;Plumbing installations in the Philippines must comply with the National Plumbing Code (NPC) and local LGU plumbing permit requirements. BuildRight Depot recommends engaging a licensed Master Plumber for installations. This compatibility verification is for material selection assistance only and does not constitute a plumbing design.&quot;; (c) for customers needing installation, system offers referral to licensed plumber partners per W904 (contractor referral service); (d) estimate saved to customer loyalty account; (e) system offers to schedule a store-level plumbing consultation appointment for complex projects requiring W989 (plumbing layout design)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1083_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1083_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1083_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1083_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: imported non-BSP fixtures flagged at POS with the required adapter SKU before sale
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1083_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1083_Annotation11" targetRef="W1083_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow13" sourceRef="W1083_Start4" targetRef="W1083_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow14" sourceRef="W1083_Task5" targetRef="W1083_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow15" sourceRef="W1083_Task6" targetRef="W1083_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow16" sourceRef="W1083_Task7" targetRef="W1083_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow17" sourceRef="W1083_Task8" targetRef="W1083_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1083_Flow18" sourceRef="W1083_Task9" targetRef="W1083_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
