    <bpmn:process id="W_W1084" name="W1084. Customer Home Security &amp; CCTV System Design &amp; Product Recommendation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests a home security system design, CCTV camera layout, or burglar alarm system recommendation for residential or small commercial property
Frequency: ~2,000–3,500 customer interactions/month across all stores (growing segment driven by Philippine crime rates and affordable IP camera technology)
Volume: 1 system design per customer visit
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1084 — Customer Home Security &amp; CCTV System Design &amp; Product Recommendation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1084_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1084_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1084_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1084_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1084_Start4" name="Customer requests a home security system design, CCTV camera layout, or burglar alarm…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1084_Task5" name="Property Assessment &amp; Security Requirements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Property Assessment &amp; Security Requirements: Sales Associate gathers property and security details: (a) property type: single-detached house, townhouse, condominium, apartment, small commercial (store, workshop, office); (b) property size: lot area (sqm), number of floors, perimeter length (meters); (c) entry points: number of doors (main, back, side, garage), number of ground-floor windows, garage/carport presence; (d) security priorities: perimeter monitoring, entry point detection, indoor monitoring, vehicle monitoring, nanny/caregiver monitoring; (e) remote access requirement: customer wants to view cameras from mobile phone (yes/no), frequency of remote viewing, number of household members who need access; (f) internet connectivity: WiFi available (speed if known), wired Ethernet availability at planned camera locations, cellular signal strength (for 4G cameras in remote areas); (g) power availability: outlets near planned camera locations, willingness to run new electrical wiring; (h) budget range: entry-level (PHP 3,000–8,000), mid-range (PHP 8,000–20,000), premium (PHP 20,000–50,000+)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1084_Task6" name="CCTV Camera Layout &amp; Coverage Design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CCTV Camera Layout &amp; Coverage Design: System generates camera placement plan: (a) perimeter cameras: one camera per 8–10 meters of boundary wall/fence coverage, mounted at 2.5–3m height, wide-angle lens (2.8mm for 100° FOV or 3.6mm for 85° FOV); (b) entry point cameras: dedicated camera for each main door and vehicle gate; (c) outdoor cameras: IP67 weather-rated minimum, IR night vision range ≥ 20m, true WDR (wide dynamic range) for backlit entrances; (d) indoor cameras: for monitoring main living areas, choose dome-style (less obtrusive) with 2.8mm lens; (e) camera resolution recommendation based on budget: 2MP (1080p) minimum for general monitoring, 4MP/5MP for license plate recognition at gates, 8MP (4K) for premium detail; (f) special cameras: PTZ (pan-tilt-zoom) for large open areas, doorbell camera (WiFi) for main entrance, 4G solar camera for areas without power/WiFi; (g) system outputs a camera count and a recommended placement floor plan sketch
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1084_Task7" name="Recording, Storage &amp; Network Design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Recording, Storage &amp; Network Design: System specifies recording infrastructure: (a) NVR (network video recorder) channel count = camera count + 20% spare capacity for future expansion; (b) storage calculation: recording days desired × cameras × bitrate × hours/day ÷ 8 ÷ 1024 = TB required (typical: 4 cameras at 2Mbps ≈ 648 GB/camera/month → ~2.6 TB total → 3TB surveillance-rated HDD minimum); (c) HDD selection: surveillance-rated HDD (WD Purple, Seagate SkyHawk) required (standard desktop HDDs fail under 24/7 write load); (d) network design: for IP cameras on existing WiFi — max 2–3 cameras per WiFi access point to avoid bandwidth congestion; for 4+ cameras — recommend PoE (Power over Ethernet) NVR with built-in PoE switch for reliability; (e) remote viewing: system confirms mobile app compatibility (iOS/Android), cloud storage options (optional subscription), and router configuration requirements (port forwarding or P2P cloud access)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–4 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1084_Task8" name="Alarm &amp; Accessory Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Alarm &amp; Accessory Selection: System recommends complementary security components: (a) door/window magnetic contact sensors for entry point detection; (b) PIR (passive infrared) motion sensors for indoor zones; (c) siren/strobe alarm (120dB minimum for audible deterrence); (d) smart lock for main door (fingerprint, PIN, RFID, or Bluetooth); (e) UPS (uninterruptible power supply) for NVR and network — critical in Philippines where power outages are common and burglars may cut power; (f) cable accessories: Cat6 Ethernet cable (for PoE cameras), power extension cables, cable conduits, junction boxes; (g) mounting hardware: camera brackets, pole mounts, cable clips; (h) system recommends installation tools: drill, Ethernet crimper, fish tape, cable tester
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–4 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1084_Task9" name="Complete System BOM, Estimate &amp; Advisory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Complete System BOM, Estimate &amp; Advisory: (a) system generates complete BOM with itemized pricing: cameras, NVR, HDD, cables, sensors, accessories, UPS, tools; (b) for trade/B2B customers, applies contract pricing per W163; (c) estimate includes: camera count summary, storage capacity confirmation, network requirement summary, estimated installation time (DIY: 4–8 hours for 4-camera system; professional: 1–2 days); (d) advisory printed: &quot;CCTV installation is not regulated in the Philippines for residential use. However, cameras must not be pointed at neighboring properties&#x27; private areas. Audio recording without consent may violate RA 10173 (Data Privacy Act). BuildRight Depot recommends professional installation for optimal camera positioning and cable management.&quot;; (e) system offers referral to licensed security system installers per W904; (f) estimate saved to customer loyalty account
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1084_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1084_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1084_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1084_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: is offline during outages — precisely when break-ins may occur; operational: must enforce surveillance-HDD-only recommendation
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
