    <bpmn:process id="W_W1089" name="W1089. Store-Level Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Digital Room Visualizer Kiosk Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer visits the tile &amp; flooring gallery and requests visual preview of tile options in a room setting, or Sales Associate proactively directs customer to the visualizer kiosk during tile selection
Frequency: ~6,000–10,000 kiosk sessions/month across all stores (tiles &amp; flooring represent 12% of SKUs, ~4,200 items, and are one of the highest-value per-unit categories)
Volume: 1 room visualization per session (customer may run 2–3 sessions per visit)
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tiles &amp; Flooring Section)
Participants: Sales Associate (Tiles Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1089 — Store-Level Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Digital Room Visualizer Kiosk Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1089_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1089_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1089_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1089_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1089_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1089_Start5" name="Customer visits the tile &amp; flooring gallery and requests visual preview of tile options…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1089_Task6" name="Customer Onboarding &amp; Room Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Onboarding &amp; Room Setup: (a) Sales Associate welcomes customer to tile visualizer kiosk; (b) customer selects room type from templates: bathroom, kitchen, living room, bedroom, outdoor patio, commercial/office, or custom (upload own photo via QR code); (c) customer enters room dimensions (length × width in meters) or selects from common Filipino room sizes; (d) customer selects surface to visualize: floor only, walls only, floor + accent wall, or floor + all walls; (e) system loads 3D room model with selected dimensions and surface areas
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1089_Task7" name="Tile Selection &amp; Real-Time Visualization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tile Selection &amp; Real-Time Visualization: (a) customer browses tile options on the kiosk: filter by collection, color, material, size, price range, and SRP per piece/sqm; (b) system displays only tiles currently in stock at the specific store per W533 (real-time inventory); out-of-stock tiles shown grayed out with &quot;available at DC — 2-day delivery&quot; option; (c) customer taps a tile to apply it to the room surface: system renders the tile pattern in real-time with correct scale, grout line width (typically 2–3mm), and tile layout pattern (straight/break-joint, diagonal, herringbone, brick-bond); (d) customer can view different tile combinations: e.g., floor tile + wall tile + accent border tile, each independently selectable; (e) system provides 360° rotation and zoom for the rendered room; (f) Associate offers design guidance: &quot;For small bathrooms, lighter colors and larger format tiles make the space feel bigger. The 60×60cm tiles with fewer grout lines are trending for modern Filipino homes.&quot;; (g) customer may save multiple design options to compare side-by-side
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1089_Task8" name="Companion Material Auto-Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Companion Material Auto-Calculation: System automatically calculates the full material list based on the selected tile design and room dimensions: (a) floor tile quantity = room area (sqm) ÷ tile coverage per piece × 1.10 (10% wastage) — rounded up to full boxes; (b) wall tile quantity = wall area (sqm) ÷ tile coverage per piece × 1.10 — minus door and window openings; (c) tile adhesive quantity = area (sqm) × 4–5 kg/sqm (depending on tile size and trowel notch); (d) grout quantity = area (sqm) × 0.3–0.5 kg/sqm (depending on grout line width and tile thickness); (e) waterproofing for bathroom walls (mandatory in Philippine construction): area × 1.5 kg/sqm × 2 coats; (f) tile spacers (2mm or 3mm): 1 bag per 5 sqm; (g) tiling tools: notched trowel, rubber grout float, tile cutter (manual or rental per W139), sponge, bucket; (h) for outdoor tiles: drainage mat and cement board underlayment if specified; (i) system calculates total estimated cost of materials; (j) for trade accounts, applies contract pricing per W163
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1089_Task9" name="Design Save, Estimate &amp; Sharing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Design Save, Estimate &amp; Sharing: (a) customer saves visualization to their loyalty account — accessible via mobile app or web for later review; (b) system generates a PDF estimate containing: room visualization render (before/after), itemized material list with quantities and prices, total estimated cost, tile specifications (material, size, finish, SRP per piece and per sqm), store inventory availability per line item, and estimated delivery timeline for DC-sourced items; (c) customer can share visualization via email, Viber, or Messenger (popular in the Philippines) to show family members or contractor; (d) customer can request a printed copy at the kiosk (thermal printer attached); (e) system offers conversion to project quotation per W162 for B2B/trade customers; (f) estimate is linked to customer loyalty account and tagged with &quot;Visualizer Lead&quot; for follow-up per W756 (post-purchase follow-up adapted for pre-purchase)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1089_Task10" name="Kiosk Maintenance &amp; Content Updates">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Kiosk Maintenance &amp; Content Updates: (a) daily: Sales Associate powers on kiosk at store opening, verifies touchscreen calibration, checks network connectivity, and confirms tile catalog synchronization with ERP inventory per W533; (b) weekly: Associate cleans kiosk screen and enclosure, checks printer paper and ink, and verifies that the latest tile products and pricing are loaded (sync with merchandising system per W50 PIM); (c) monthly: IT support per W265 (POS terminal hardware maintenance adapted for kiosk) performs software update, cache clearing, and diagnostic check; (d) quarterly: tile catalog content refresh — new product images loaded, discontinued products removed per W68 (product lifecycle &amp; discontinuation), new room templates added based on Philippine design trends; (e) usage analytics: system tracks kiosk sessions per store, conversion rate (sessions → tile purchases), average time per session, most-viewed tile collections, and abandonment rate; data used by Category Manager to optimize tile assortment per W1 (merchandise planning &amp; assortment review)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / IT Support
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Daily: 5 min; Weekly: 15 min; Monthly: 30 min; Quarterly: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1089_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1089_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1089_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1089_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Tiles &amp; Flooring Section) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tiles &amp; Flooring Section)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1089_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1089_Annotation12" targetRef="W1089_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1089_Flow14" sourceRef="W1089_Start5" targetRef="W1089_Task6" />
