    <bpmn:process id="W_W1090" name="W1090. Customer HVAC Ductwork Design &amp; Complete Material Sizing Recommendation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests a complete air conditioning system design including ductwork layout for a residential or small commercial project, or the consultation from W985 (aircon BTU calculation) identifies a ducted/central system requirement
Frequency: ~800–1,500 consultations/month across all stores (ducted systems are less common than split/window units but represent high-value projects averaging PHP 80,000–300,000)
Volume: 1 system design per consultation
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Appliance/Electrical Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1090 — Customer HVAC Ductwork Design &amp; Complete Material Sizing Recommendation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1090_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1090_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1090_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1090_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1090_Start4" name="Customer requests a complete air conditioning system design including ductwork layout for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1090_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1090_Task5" name="Project Assessment &amp; Room-by-Room Load Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Assessment &amp; Room-by-Room Load Calculation: (a) Sales Associate gathers project details: property type (residential or commercial), total floor area, number of rooms/zones, ceiling type (drop ceiling/T-bar with space for ducts, or concrete slab — slab limits ductwork options), outdoor unit placement options (roof access, ground-level pad, balcony), and whether the customer wants a single-zone or multi-zone system; (b) for each room/zone: room dimensions, window area and orientation (west-facing rooms have higher solar gain in the Philippines), insulation level (uninsulated Philippine hollow block walls vs. insulated), occupancy, and heat-generating equipment (computers, kitchen appliances, lighting); (c) system performs ASHRAE-based cooling load calculation per room: total load (BTU/hr) = sensible load + latent load; (d) system selects ducted indoor unit capacity: matches total cooling load across all zones; available capacities: 18,000 BTU (1.5 HP), 24,000 BTU (2 HP), 36,000 BTU (3 HP), 48,000 BTU (4 HP), 60,000 BTU (5 HP); (e) system selects condensing unit to match
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1090_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1090_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1090_Task6" name="Ductwork Layout &amp; Sizing Design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ductwork Layout &amp; Sizing Design: System designs the air distribution system: (a) for each room/zone: calculates required airflow (CFM) = room cooling load (BTU/hr) ÷ (1.085 × temperature difference, typically 20°F for Philippine conditions); (b) main trunk duct size: total CFM ÷ max velocity (1,200 FPM) = duct area (sq ft); select standard rectangular duct size (e.g., 20&quot;×8&quot;, 24&quot;×10&quot;) or round flex duct diameter; (c) branch duct to each room: room CFM ÷ max velocity (800 FPM) = branch duct area; select flex duct diameter (6&quot;, 8&quot;, 10&quot;, or 12&quot;); (d) supply air diffuser/register per room: size based on CFM at ≤ 300 FPM face velocity (quiet operation); select from BuildRight inventory: 4-way ceiling diffuser, 2-way supply register, or linear slot diffuser; (e) return air grille: total system CFM ÷ 400 FPM = return grille area; position in central hallway or above ceiling; (f) duct insulation: for ducts in ceiling space (hot zone), specify 25mm or 50mm thick foil-faced fiberglass or elastomeric insulation (available from BuildRight per W1057 insulation calculator); (g) system generates a simple duct layout schematic showing trunk, branches, and terminal locations
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1090_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1090_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1090_Task7" name="Complete Material List &amp; Refrigerant Piping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Complete Material List &amp; Refrigerant Piping: System generates full BOM: (a) Ducted indoor unit (capacity matched per step 1); (b) Condensing unit (outdoor unit, matched capacity); (c) Refrigerant piping: copper tubing — liquid line (¼&quot; or ⅜&quot;) + suction line (½&quot;, ⅝&quot;, or ¾&quot;) based on distance between indoor and outdoor units; pre-flared connections or flare tool for on-site flaring; (d) Insulation for refrigerant piping (closed-cell elastomeric, ¾&quot; wall thickness); (e) Flexible insulated ductwork: main trunk length + branch lengths per layout design; (f) Duct fittings: elbows, Y-branches, reducers, take-offs; (g) Ceiling diffusers/registers (per room); (h) Return air grille + filter; (i) Condensate drain: PVC pipe (½&quot; or ¾&quot;) from indoor unit drain pan to nearest drain point + PVC insulation (to prevent condensation dripping); (j) Drain pump (if indoor unit is below the drain point); (k) Electrical: dedicated circuit breaker per W1064, electrical cable (THHN wire in EMT conduit), disconnect switch at outdoor unit; (l) Control: wall-mounted thermostat (manual or smart WiFi thermostat), zone dampers (if multi-zone); (m) Mounting hardware: indoor unit ceiling mounting frame, outdoor unit wall bracket or roof curb, vibration isolators, rubber pads; (n) Accessories: refrigerant gas (R32 or R410A, per unit specification), vacuum pump rental (per W139 tool rental), manifold gauge set; (o) installation materials: sealant, duct tape (foil tape), mechanical fasteners, copper joint compound
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1090_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1090_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1090_Task8" name="Estimate, Installation Advisory &amp; Professional Referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate, Installation Advisory &amp; Professional Referral: (a) system generates itemized estimate with duct schematic and complete BOM; (b) total estimated cost ranges: PHP 80,000–150,000 for a 2 HP ducted system (residential, 2–3 rooms), PHP 150,000–300,000 for a 5 HP ducted system (large residential or small commercial, 4–6 rooms); (c) installation advisory: &quot;Ducted air conditioning system installation requires: (1) Licensed Mechanical Engineer for ductwork design certification (required by LGU building permit office for commercial installations); (2) TESDA-certified (Refrigeration and Air-Conditioning NC II) technician for refrigerant handling; (3) Licensed electrical engineer for electrical connection per Philippine Electrical Code. This material list is for estimation only. BuildRight Depot recommends engaging a qualified HVAC contractor for installation.&quot;; (d) system offers referral to HVAC installation partners per W904 (contractor referral); (e) for trade/B2B customers: estimate converts to project quote per W162 with staged delivery scheduling per W164
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1090_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1090_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1090_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1090_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1090_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate on ducted-system design consultations
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1090_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1090_Annotation10" targetRef="W1090_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
