    <bpmn:process id="W_W1093" name="W1093. Customer Interior Paint Color Scheme Consultation &amp; Material Board Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer visits the paint section and requests help selecting a color scheme for a room or entire house, or Sales Associate identifies that the customer is planning a multi-room painting project during the initial paint mixing consultation per W168
Frequency: ~5,000–8,000 consultations/month across all stores (paint &amp; finishes represent 8% of SKUs, ~2,800 items; interior painting is one of the most common home improvement projects in the Philippines)
Volume: 1 color scheme consultation per customer visit
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint Section)
Participants: Sales Associate (Paint Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1093 — Customer Interior Paint Color Scheme Consultation &amp; Material Board Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1093_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1093_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1093_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1093_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1093_Start4" name="Customer visits the paint section and requests help selecting a color scheme for a room…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1093_Task5" name="Project Scope &amp; Room Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Scope &amp; Room Assessment: Sales Associate gathers painting project details: (a) project scope: single room, multiple rooms, full house interior, or full house interior + exterior; (b) for each room: room name (living room, bedroom, kitchen, bathroom, hallway), room dimensions (floor area in sqm, wall height — standard Philippine ceiling height: 2.4–2.7m), condition of existing paint (new surface, previously painted in good condition, previously painted with stains/damage); (c) customer&#x27;s style preference: modern minimalist (neutrals, whites, grays), Scandinavian (light pastels, whites), tropical Filipino (warm earth tones, muted greens and blues), industrial (dark grays, charcoals), or traditional (cream, beige, warm whites); (d) existing fixed elements that constrain color choice: floor tile color, furniture color, kitchen cabinet color, window frames; (e) budget range for paint materials
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1093_Task6" name="Color Scheme Design &amp; Visualization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Color Scheme Design &amp; Visualization: (a) Sales Associate uses paint brand color deck/fan deck to present curated color palettes matching customer&#x27;s style preference: 3–5 palette options, each with a primary wall color, secondary/accent wall color, ceiling white, and trim color; (b) system provides room visualization via tablet: apply selected palette to a room template showing wall color, accent wall, ceiling, and trim; (c) for each palette, Associate explains: (i) primary color coverage (all walls except accent wall), (ii) accent wall application (typically one wall — the wall behind the headboard in bedrooms, or the TV wall in living rooms), (iii) ceiling treatment (standard ceiling white or tinted ceiling for dramatic effect), (iv) trim and door color (white, matching wall color, or contrasting); (d) customer selects preferred palette; (e) for multi-room projects: Associate ensures color flow between rooms — adjacent rooms should share at least one color element for visual cohesion; system offers &quot;whole house&quot; color journey recommendations (e.g., progressing from light neutrals in entry/living areas to deeper tones in private spaces)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1093_Task7" name="Surface Preparation Assessment &amp; Primer Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Surface Preparation Assessment &amp; Primer Selection: System evaluates surface preparation needs based on customer&#x27;s wall condition: (a) New concrete/plaster walls (common in new Philippine construction): require alkali-resistant primer to prevent lime/salt efflorescence — specify 1 coat of Boysen Permacoat Primer, Davies Alkali Resisting Primer, or equivalent; (b) Previously painted walls (good condition): spot-putty any nail holes or cracks, light sanding, no primer needed if existing paint is sound; (c) Previously painted walls (stained or damaged): stain-blocking primer (water stains from leaks — common in Philippine homes due to rainy season, smoke stains from kitchen, crayon/marker from children); (d) Chalking old paint: bind chalking surface with oil-based or water-based primer-sealer before repainting; (e) Concrete patches/putty: wall putty ( Boysen Wall Putty or equivalent) for smoothing rough areas, applied after primer, sanded smooth before topcoat; (f) system calculates putty quantity based on estimated wall area needing repair; (g) for each surface type, system adds appropriate primer and preparation materials to the BOM
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1093_Task8" name="Complete Material List &amp; Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Complete Material List &amp; Quantity Calculation: System generates full paint BOM: (a) for each room: (i) wall area = perimeter × ceiling height − door area (1.6 sqm per door) − window area; (ii) paint quantity = wall area ÷ coverage per liter (typically 10–12 sqm per liter per coat for interior latex) × number of coats (2 coats standard, 3 coats for dramatic color change); (iii) ceiling paint = ceiling area ÷ coverage × 2 coats; (iv) trim paint = linear meters of trim ÷ coverage per liter × 2 coats; (b) paint grouped by color across all rooms (same color in multiple rooms combined into single line item); (c) for each paint product: system selects the appropriate finish: matte or satin for living room/bedroom walls, semi-gloss or satin for kitchen/bathroom walls, gloss or semi-gloss for trim/doors; (d) companion materials: primer (type and quantity per step 3), wall putty (kg), sandpaper (sheets by grit: 80 for rough, 120 for smooth, 220 for finish), painter&#x27;s tape (width: 1&quot; or 2&quot;, number of rolls), paint rollers (9&quot; for walls, 4&quot; for trim, foam roller for smooth finish), paint brushes (2&quot; for cutting in, 4&quot; for broad areas), roller tray and refill, drop cloth/plastic sheeting (floor protection), roller extension pole (for high ceilings); (e) system calculates total estimated cost and estimated project duration (DIY: room painting takes ~1 day per coat per room; professional: 1–2 days per room)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1093_Task9" name="Material Board Assembly &amp; Estimate Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Material Board Assembly &amp; Estimate Generation: (a) Sales Associate assembles a physical &quot;material board&quot; for the customer: paint color swatches (from brand fan deck or painted sample chips per W903 sample loan program), selected primer chip, and a printed summary of the color scheme; (b) system generates PDF estimate with: color palette visual, room-by-room paint assignments, complete material list with quantities and prices, total estimated cost, and estimated project duration; (c) system links the color selections to the customer&#x27;s loyalty account for future reorder: &quot;When you need to repaint or touch up, your exact colors are saved in your BuildRight account.&quot;; (d) for customers who want to proceed immediately: Associate processes the paint mixing order per W168 — each color mixed by the tinting machine per the brand&#x27;s color code; (e) for customers who want to test colors first: system offers sample-size paint cans (250ml or 500ml trial sizes, available from major brands) for at-home testing before committing to full quantities; (f) advisory: &quot;Paint colors may appear different on your walls due to lighting conditions. BuildRight recommends testing a 1m × 1m area on your wall and viewing it at different times of day before committing to the full project.&quot;; (g) system offers referral to professional painter partners per W904 for customers who prefer not to DIY
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1093_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1093_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1093_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1093_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must lock color codes to the specific brand&#x27;s mixing formula; operational: must clearly show cost per coat to set expectations
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint Section)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1093_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1093_Annotation11" targetRef="W1093_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1093_Flow13" sourceRef="W1093_Start4" targetRef="W1093_Task5" />
