    <bpmn:process id="W_W1095" name="W1095. Store-Level Customer Electrical Residential Wiring Diagram &amp; Material List Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests a complete residential electrical wiring layout and material list for a new home construction or major renovation project, extending from the panel board design in W1064
Frequency: ~2,500–4,000 consultations/month across all stores (electrical is 10% of SKUs, ~3,500 items; new residential construction and renovation are core customer projects)
Volume: 1 wiring diagram and material list per consultation
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1095 — Store-Level Customer Electrical Residential Wiring Diagram &amp; Material List Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1095_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1095_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1095_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1095_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1095_Start4" name="Customer requests a complete residential electrical wiring layout and material list for a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1095_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1095_Task5" name="Floor Plan Input &amp; Room Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Floor Plan Input &amp; Room Specification: (a) Sales Associate enters the customer&#x27;s floor plan into the system: number of floors, room layout (living room, dining room, kitchen, bedrooms, bathrooms, laundry area, garage/carport, outdoor area); (b) for each room, Associate specifies: room name, dimensions, and electrical point requirements: (i) ceiling light points (quantity, type: flush mount, pendant, LED panel); (ii) wall light points (quantity, if any); (iii) switch locations (quantity, type: 1-gang, 2-gang, 3-gang, position: inside or outside room); (iv) convenience outlets (quantity, type: grounded duplex, USB combo, weatherproof for outdoor); (v) special outlets (air conditioner — wall-mounted at 1.8m, electric stove — floor-level, water heater — wall-mounted, washing machine — floor-level); (vi) exhaust fan points (bathroom, kitchen); (vii) doorbell point (main entrance); (c) for outdoor: perimeter light points, gate light, garage light, outdoor outlets (GFCI-protected)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1095_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1095_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1095_Task6" name="Automatic Circuit Allocation &amp; Wiring Diagram Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automatic Circuit Allocation &amp; Wiring Diagram Generation: System performs PEC-compliant circuit allocation: (a) lighting circuits: allocate points to 15A circuits with max 10 light points per circuit per PEC; separate lighting circuits per floor; (b) convenience outlet circuits: allocate to 20A circuits with max 6 outlets per circuit per PEC; separate kitchen and bathroom outlet circuits; (c) dedicated appliance circuits per W1064 (aircon, water heater, electric stove, pump); (d) system generates single-line wiring diagram: shows panel board at top, circuits branching down to room-level junction boxes, then to individual points; (e) wire routing: system estimates wire lengths based on room layout: (i) home run length from panel to each room&#x27;s first junction box (estimated from floor plan dimensions); (ii) branch lengths within each room between points; (iii) standard factor: total wire per circuit = measured length × 1.3 (30% additional for routing around obstacles, drops, and connections); (f) system selects wire size per circuit per W982: 14 AWG (2.0 sqmm) for 15A lighting circuits, 12 AWG (3.5 sqmm) for 20A outlet circuits, 10 AWG (5.5 sqmm) for 30A appliance circuits, 8 AWG (8.0 sqmm) for 40A circuits, 6 AWG (14 sqmm) for 50–60A circuits
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1095_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1095_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1095_Task7" name="Complete Electrical Material List">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Complete Electrical Material List: System generates comprehensive BOM: (a) Wire/Cable: per circuit — wire size, number of conductors (2-wire with ground for 1-phase circuits, or 3-wire with ground for multi-wire branch circuits), length per circuit in meters (rounded up to standard roll lengths: 100m rolls for 14/12 AWG, 50m rolls for 10/8/6 AWG); (b) Conduit: EMT (electrical metallic tubing) or PVC conduit per circuit — diameter (½&quot; for 2 wires, ¾&quot; for 3–4 wires, 1&quot; for 5+ wires per PEC fill ratio), length per circuit; conduit fittings: connectors, couplings, elbows, straps; (c) Boxes: junction boxes (4&quot; octagonal for ceiling points, 4&quot; square for switch/outlet combinations, handy boxes for exposed wiring), switch boxes (gang count matching switch type), outlet boxes, ceiling rose/canopy for light fixtures; (d) Switches: per room specification — 1-gang, 2-gang, 3-gang toggle or rocker switches, 1-way and 2-way (for hallways and stairs), dimmer switches (optional, for living room/bedroom); (e) Outlets: grounded duplex convenience outlets (per room count), USB combo outlets (optional upgrade), GFCI outlets (bathroom, kitchen, outdoor, garage), weatherproof covers for outdoor outlets; (f) Circuit breakers: per W1064 panel schedule; (g) Service entrance: meter base (MERALCO/Davao Light approved), service entrance wire (size per utility requirement), grounding system (ground rod, ground wire, ground clamp); (h) Accessories: wire nuts/solderless connectors, electrical tape (per circuit count), cable ties, nail-in clips for conduit, drywall anchors for boxes, circuit directory labels for panel; (i) Installation tools: wire stripper, conduit cutter, fish tape, voltage tester, screwdrivers (flat and Phillips), drill with masonry bit for concrete walls
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1095_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1095_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1095_Task8" name="Estimate, Safety Advisory &amp; Professional Referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate, Safety Advisory &amp; Professional Referral: (a) system generates itemized estimate with: single-line wiring diagram, room-by-room circuit allocation table, complete BOM with quantities and prices, total estimated cost; (b) system calculates estimated cost breakdown: wire and cable (~40% of electrical material cost), conduit and fittings (~15%), switches and outlets (~15%), boxes (~10%), circuit breakers and panel (~15%), accessories (~5%); (c) for trade account customers: applies contract pricing per W163 and converts to project quote per W162; (d) safety advisory: &quot;All electrical installations in the Philippines must comply with the Philippine Electrical Code (PEC) 2017 and must be performed by a licensed Professional Electrical Engineer (PEE) or Registered Master Electrician (RME) under the supervision of a PEE. This wiring diagram and material list is for quantity estimation only and does not constitute a professional electrical design. A licensed PEE must review and approve the electrical plan before construction. BuildRight Depot requires customers to engage a qualified electrical professional for installation.&quot;; (e) system offers referral to licensed electrical engineers and electricians per W904; (f) estimate and diagram saved to customer loyalty account for future reference
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1095_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1095_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1095_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1095_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1095_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must calculate and enforce PEC conduit fill ratios
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1095_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1095_Annotation10" targetRef="W1095_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
