    <bpmn:process id="W_W1096" name="W1096. Customer Solar Water Heater System Sizing &amp; Complete Package Recommendation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquires about solar water heating options, or Sales Associate identifies solar water heater applicability during a water heater consultation or solar panel consultation per W990
Frequency: ~600–1,200 consultations/month across all stores (growing segment driven by Philippine electricity costs and DOE renewable energy promotion)
Volume: 1 system design per consultation
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Electrical/Appliance Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1096 — Customer Solar Water Heater System Sizing &amp; Complete Package Recommendation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1096_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1096_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1096_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1096_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1096_Start4" name="Customer inquires about solar water heating options, or Sales Associate identifies solar…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1096_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1096_Task5" name="Hot Water Demand Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Hot Water Demand Assessment: Sales Associate gathers hot water usage information: (a) household size (number of persons); (b) bathrooms with hot water: count and type (shower only, shower + bathtub); (c) kitchen hot water: yes/no (sink hot water tap); (d) laundry hot water: yes/no (washing machine hot water connection); (e) hot water usage pattern: morning peak (bathing), evening peak (bathing + kitchen), or both; (f) current water heating method: electric storage, electric tankless, LPG, or none; (g) desired water temperature (comfortable shower: 38–42°C); (h) cold water inlet temperature: Philippine municipal water ~25–28°C, deep well ~26–29°C; (i) roof type and orientation: flat concrete roof or pitched roof (G.I. sheet or tile), orientation (south-facing optimal in Philippines), available roof area for collector; (j) roof structural capacity: solar water heater + water tank = 150–300 kg — Filipino concrete flat roofs can typically support this, but lightweight G.I. sheet roofs may require structural reinforcement
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1096_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1096_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1096_Task6" name="System Sizing &amp; Technology Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System Sizing &amp; Technology Selection: System performs sizing calculation: (a) daily hot water demand: standard Philippine household usage = 40–50 liters per person per day at 50°C delivery temperature; total = household size × 50 liters; (b) collector area: Philippine solar radiation ≈ 5 kWh/m²/day; collector area = daily hot water demand (liters) × temperature rise (°C) ÷ (solar radiation × collector efficiency × conversion factor); typical result: 1 sqm collector per 50–70 liters of daily hot water demand; (c) tank size = daily hot water demand × 1.2 (20% buffer for cloudy day storage); (d) system recommendations based on household size: (i) 2–3 persons: 150L tank + 1.5–2 sqm collector (20-tube ETC or 1.5 sqm FPC); (ii) 4–5 persons: 250L tank + 3–4 sqm collector (30-tube ETC or 2 × 2 sqm FPC); (iii) 6–8 persons: 300L tank + 4–5 sqm collector (2 × 20-tube ETC or 2 × 2.5 sqm FPC); (e) technology selection: ETC recommended for households in cloudy areas (mountainous regions, typhoon-prone areas), FPC recommended for most Philippine lowland locations (more durable, lower maintenance); (f) passive vs. active: passive (thermosiphon) recommended for single-story homes with flat concrete roof (tank + collector on roof); active (pumped) recommended for multi-story homes or roofs that cannot support tank weight (tank at ground level, collector on roof)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1096_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1096_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1096_Task7" name="Complete System Package &amp; Companion Materials">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Complete System Package &amp; Companion Materials: System generates full BOM: (a) solar collector: ETC (specify tube count, diameter, length) or FPC (specify dimensions, absorber coating, glazing type); (b) hot water storage tank: capacity, stainless steel or enamel-lined, insulation thickness (≥50mm polyurethane foam), integrated or separate from collector; (c) mounting frame: stainless steel or aluminum, adjustable tilt angle (optimal tilt for Philippines: 10–15° for year-round performance, adjustable for seasonal optimization); (d) circulation pump (active system only): rated for hot water, 40–60W, with controller; (e) piping: insulated hot water pipe (PPR or copper, minimum 19mm diameter, with 19mm foam insulation per W1057); (f) cold water supply connection: PPR pipe from existing cold water line to tank inlet; (g) hot water delivery connection: PPR or copper pipe from tank outlet to bathrooms and kitchen; (h) temperature &amp; pressure relief valve (safety device per PEC/plumbing code); (i) anti-scale filter (for areas with hard water — some Philippine water supplies have high mineral content); (j) backup electric heating element: most solar water heater tanks include a 1.5–2kW electric backup element for cloudy/rainy days when solar is insufficient; (k) accessories: pipe insulation, pipe fittings, valves (gate valve, check valve), mounting hardware (bolts, anchors for concrete roof, flashing for pitched roof), sealant, and thermostatic mixing valve (prevents scalding at taps)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1096_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1096_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1096_Task8" name="ROI Calculation, Estimate &amp; Installation Advisory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: ROI Calculation, Estimate &amp; Installation Advisory: (a) system calculates financial return: (i) current electric water heater energy cost: liters/day × temperature rise × specific heat of water ÷ electric heater efficiency × PHP/kWh rate = monthly cost; (ii) solar water heater energy cost: PHP 0 (sunlight is free) + backup electric heating on cloudy days (~20% of total energy) = monthly cost; (iii) monthly savings = (i) − (ii); (iv) payback period = system cost ÷ monthly savings; typical result: PHP 25,000–45,000 system cost ÷ PHP 2,000–4,000/month savings = 6–18 month payback; (b) system generates estimate with: system specification, complete BOM, total cost, ROI analysis, estimated installation time (1–2 days for passive system, 2–3 days for active system); (c) installation advisory: &quot;Solar water heater installation involves both plumbing and structural work. Tank and collector mounting on the roof requires proper waterproofing to prevent leaks. BuildRight Depot recommends professional installation by a qualified plumber and, for active systems, a licensed electrician for the pump/controller wiring.&quot;; (d) system offers referral to accredited installation partners per W904; (e) for customers interested in larger renewable energy systems: Associate mentions W990 (solar PV system) for electricity generation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Electrical Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1096_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1096_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1096_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1096_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1096_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must flag structural assessment requirement
Owner: Electrical Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1096_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1096_Annotation10" targetRef="W1096_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1096_Flow12" sourceRef="W1096_Start4" targetRef="W1096_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1096_Flow13" sourceRef="W1096_Task5" targetRef="W1096_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1096_Flow14" sourceRef="W1096_Task6" targetRef="W1096_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1096_Flow15" sourceRef="W1096_Task7" targetRef="W1096_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1096_Flow16" sourceRef="W1096_Task8" targetRef="W1096_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1096_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1096_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1096">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1096_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1096_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1096_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1096_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
