    <bpmn:process id="W_W1097" name="W1097. Store-Level Customer Outdoor Deck, Patio &amp; Pergola Material Estimation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests material estimation for an outdoor deck, patio, or pergola project, or Sales Associate identifies the project type during a lumber or garden section consultation
Frequency: ~2,000–3,500 consultations/month across all stores (outdoor living is a growing segment in the Philippine market, particularly in upscale subdivisions and resort areas)
Volume: 1 structure estimation per consultation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Lumber Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1097 — Store-Level Customer Outdoor Deck, Patio &amp; Pergola Material Estimation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1097_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1097_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1097_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1097_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1097_Start4" name="Customer requests material estimation for an outdoor deck, patio, or pergola project, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1097_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1097_Task5" name="Structure Design &amp; Dimension Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Structure Design &amp; Dimension Input: Sales Associate gathers project specifications: (a) structure type: deck only, pergola only, deck + pergola, patio (concrete slab); (b) deck dimensions: length × width × height above ground (ground-level: 0–0.3m, raised: 0.3–1.0m, elevated: 1.0m+); (c) deck shape: rectangular, L-shaped, or multi-level; (d) deck surface material preference: natural wood (specify: tanguile, yakal, or treated pine), composite decking (WPC), or concrete tile; (e) pergola dimensions: length × width × post height (standard: 2.4m post height for 2.1m clearance); (f) pergola roof type: open-rafter (decorative only, no rain protection), polycarbonate roof (rain protection + natural light), G.I. sheet roof (full rain protection), or retractable canvas/shade sail; (g) site conditions: ground type (concrete pad, compacted soil, or grass), drainage consideration (slope away from house), attachment to existing structure (ledger board against house wall or freestanding); (h) load requirements: residential light-duty (furniture + people, ~200 kg/sqm) or heavy-duty (hot tub, outdoor kitchen, ~400 kg/sqm)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1097_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1097_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1097_Task6" name="Structural Design &amp; Material Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Structural Design &amp; Material Calculation: System designs the structure and calculates materials: For Deck: (a) footing: concrete footing at each post location — footing diameter × depth based on deck height and soil type (Philippine standard: 0.3m diameter × 0.6m depth for ground-level, 0.4m × 0.8m for raised); footing count = post grid spacing (typically 1.5–2.0m centers); (b) posts: 4×4 (100mm × 100mm) or 6×6 (150mm × 150mm) treated lumber or steel — quantity = footing count, length = deck height + footing projection + beam clearance; (c) beams: double 2×8 or 2×10 (50mm × 200mm or 50mm × 250mm) per span table — spans ≤ 3.0m for 2×8, ≤ 4.0m for 2×10; (d) joists: 2×6 or 2×8 at 400mm or 600mm spacing — quantity = deck width ÷ joist spacing + 1, length = deck depth; (e) decking boards: quantity = deck area ÷ board coverage per piece × 1.10 (10% wastage for cutting); (f) fasteners: deck screws (stainless steel 304 for coastal, 316 for saltwater proximity), joist hangers, post anchors, beam brackets, carriage bolts for post-to-beam connections. For Pergola: (g) posts: 4×4 or 6×6 — 4 posts minimum (2 per side), length = post height + footing embedment; (h) beams: double 2×8 spanning across posts; (i) rafters: 2×4 or 2×6 spanning between beams at 400–600mm spacing — quantity = pergola length ÷ rafter spacing; (j) roofing: polycarbonate sheets (6mm or 10mm twin-wall, length matching rafter span × width needed) or G.I. sheets per W983 (roofing calculator); (k) post bases: galvanized steel post anchors set in concrete footings; (l) hardware: lag bolts, through bolts, angle brackets, rafter ties
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1097_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1097_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1097_Task7" name="Companion Products &amp; Finishing Materials">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Companion Products &amp; Finishing Materials: System adds: (a) Surface preparation: gravel base under deck (for ground-level, to prevent weed growth and improve drainage) — volume in cubic meters; weed barrier fabric; (b) Concrete for footings: cement bags + sand + gravel per footing count × footing volume; concrete mix ratio per W1044; (c) Wood treatment: if using natural lumber (not pre-treated): wood preservative (solignum or equivalent), application brush, 2–3 coats recommended for ground-contact posts; (d) Deck finish: wood stain or exterior sealer for decking surface (quantity based on deck area × 2 coats); application by brush or sprayer; (e) Waterproofing: ledger board flashing (aluminum or galvanized) where deck meets house wall — prevents water infiltration; (f) Outdoor lighting: deck post solar lights, step lights (LED), pergola string lights (&quot;fairy lights&quot; — very popular in Philippine outdoor spaces), and under-deck LED strip lighting; per W1084 adapted for decorative outdoor lighting; (g) Railing (for decks &gt; 0.6m above ground per Philippine building code): posts, top rail, bottom rail, balusters (wood, steel, or cable railing), and hardware; (h) Stairs (for raised decks): stringers, treads, risers, handrail per stair calculator; (i) Tools: circular saw per W169 (lumber cutting service available in-store), drill, level, measuring tape, post level, concrete mixer rental per W1094
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–4 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1097_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1097_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1097_Task8" name="Estimate, Lumber Advisory &amp; Service Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Estimate, Lumber Advisory &amp; Service Coordination: (a) system generates itemized estimate with: structural diagram (simplified isometric sketch), complete BOM organized by structural component, quantities and prices, total estimated cost; (b) estimated cost ranges: ground-level wood deck (tanguile): PHP 2,500–4,000/sqm; raised wood deck: PHP 3,500–5,500/sqm; composite deck: PHP 5,000–8,000/sqm; pergola (wood, open-rafter): PHP 3,000–5,000/sqm; pergola (polycarbonate roof): PHP 4,500–7,000/sqm; (c) lumber advisory: (i) wood grade: per W976 (lumber grade selection) — Associate explains the difference between construction grade (knots allowed, for structural framing) and select grade (minimal knots, for visible decking and pergola beams); (ii) cutting service: per W169 — BuildRight can cut lumber to specified lengths, reducing customer&#x27;s on-site cutting; (iii) treatment: untreated lumber must be treated before installation, especially posts in contact with ground; (iv) moisture content: lumber should be kiln-dried or air-dried to ≤ 18% moisture content to prevent warping; (d) system offers installation referral per W904 for customers who need professional deck/pergola construction; (e) estimate saved to customer loyalty account
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1097_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1097_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1097_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1097_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1097_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
