    <bpmn:process id="W_W1102" name="W1102. Customer Retaining Wall &amp; Foundation Formwork Material Estimation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests material estimation for a retaining wall or foundation formwork project, or Sales Associate identifies the need during a construction material consultation for a sloped lot or multi-level project
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 consultations/month across all stores (retaining walls are common in Philippine hillside and terraced construction; foundation formwork is needed for most new construction projects)
Volume: 1 retaining wall or formwork estimation per consultation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Lumber/Building Materials Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1102 — Customer Retaining Wall &amp; Foundation Formwork Material Estimation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1102_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1102_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1102_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1102_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1102_Start4" name="Customer requests material estimation for a retaining wall or foundation formwork…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1102_Task5" name="Project Specification &amp; Structural Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Specification &amp; Structural Input: Sales Associate gathers project details: (a) For retaining walls: (i) wall height (meters) and total wall length (meters); (ii) retained soil height (may differ from wall height if wall is partially embedded); (iii) soil type: clay (high lateral pressure), sandy (moderate), gravel (low); (iv) surcharge load: is there a structure, driveway, or slope above the wall? (affects wall design); (v) wall type preference: CHB (hollow block — for walls ≤ 1.5m), reinforced concrete cantilever (for walls 1.0–3.0m), or gravity wall (stone/mass concrete — for walls ≤ 2.0m); (vi) drainage provision: weep holes (required for all retaining walls — prevents hydrostatic pressure buildup behind the wall); (b) For foundation formwork: (i) foundation type: isolated footing, continuous footing, mat foundation, or pile cap; (ii) number and dimensions of footings (length × width × depth); (iii) column dimensions and heights (from footing to beam level); (iv) beam dimensions (width × depth) and total beam length; (v) slab area and thickness (if slab formwork needed); (vi) formwork material preference: lumber (plywood + timber) — most common in the Philippines, or steel panels — for large projects; (c) Site conditions: (i) accessibility for material delivery; (ii) water table level (affects concrete mix and waterproofing needs); (iii) seismic zone per the NSCP zone map (Zone 1–4; Zone 3–4 areas drive reinforcement requirements)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1102_Task6" name="Retaining Wall Material Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Retaining Wall Material Calculation: System calculates retaining wall materials based on wall type: For CHB wall (≤ 1.5m height): (a) CHB quantity = wall area (length × height) ÷ CHB face area (0.2m × 0.4m = 0.08 sqm face area for both 4&quot; and 6&quot; CHB — the nominal size is thickness, not face) × 1.05 (5% wastage); (b) cement mortar: 1 bag cement per 70 pieces of 4&quot; CHB or 1 bag per 50 pieces of 6&quot; CHB; sand: 0.08 cubic meters per bag of cement; (c) reinforcement: for CHB walls &gt; 0.6m, vertical rebar (10mm or 12mm) at 0.40m centers grouted into CHB cells; horizontal rebar (10mm) at every 2 courses; (d) foundation: concrete strip footing below wall — width = wall height × 0.5, depth = 0.30m minimum; concrete volume per W1044; (e) drainage: weep holes (50mm PVC pipe) at 1.5m centers along wall base; gravel drain (¾&quot; crushed stone) behind the wall with filter fabric; For RC cantilever wall (1.0–3.0m): (f) concrete volume = (base slab + stem wall + toe + heel) based on standard cantilever wall proportions; system calculates per wall height; (g) reinforcement steel: main vertical bars (12mm or 16mm), horizontal distribution bars (10mm or 12mm), base slab reinforcement (12mm or 16mm both ways); rebar weight calculated per kg per W986; (h) formwork: plywood (12mm thick, 4&#x27;×8&#x27; sheets) for wall faces; timber studs (2&quot;×3&quot; at 400mm centers); timber wales (2&quot;×4&quot; at 600mm vertical spacing); form ties (snap ties or threaded rod with wing nuts); (i) concrete volume per W1044 — mix ratio 1:2:4 (Class A) for structural retaining walls; (j) drainage: perforated PVC drain pipe (110mm diameter) along wall base with gravel surround; weep holes at 1.5m centers
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1102_Task7" name="Foundation Formwork Material Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Foundation Formwork Material Calculation: System calculates formwork materials: (a) Footing formwork: (i) plywood area = 2 × (footing length + footing width) × footing depth per footing × number of footings; (ii) studs: 2&quot;×3&quot; at 400mm centers along plywood; (iii) braces: 2&quot;×4&quot; diagonal braces to prevent form bulging under concrete pressure; (iv) form ties: snap ties per lineal meter of formwork; (b) Column formwork: (i) plywood area = column perimeter × column height × number of columns; (ii) yokes/clamps: at 400mm vertical spacing (made from 2&quot;×4&quot; lumber or steel column clamps); (iii) kicker: bottom form to prevent grout leakage; (c) Beam formwork: (i) plywood area = 2 × beam depth × beam length + beam width × beam length (for soffit); (ii) soffit supports: 2&quot;×4&quot; joists at 400mm centers; (iii) shores/posts: 4&quot;×4&quot; lumber at 1.0m centers to support beam soffit; (iv) side forms: 2&quot;×3&quot; studs at 400mm centers with 2&quot;×4&quot; wales; (d) Slab formwork: (i) plywood area = slab area (sqm); (ii) joists: 2&quot;×4&quot; at 400mm centers; (iii) stringers: 2&quot;×6&quot; at 1.0m centers perpendicular to joists; (iv) shores: 4&quot;×4&quot; at 1.0m × 1.0m grid; (e) Common formwork materials: (i) form release agent (oil or emulsion — prevents concrete from sticking to plywood); (ii) nails (assorted: 2&quot; for plywood-to-stud, 3&quot; for stud-to-wale, 4&quot; for braces); (iii) tie wire (16-gauge black annealed wire for reinforcement tying); (iv) spacers: concrete cover spacers (25mm or 50mm) to maintain rebar cover; (f) lumber reuse factor: plywood = 4–5 uses (for typical construction quality), timber = 6–8 uses; system estimates new lumber purchase vs. potential reuse for customers with multiple pours
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1102_Task8" name="Companion Materials &amp; Complete BOM">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Companion Materials &amp; Complete BOM: System adds companion materials: (a) Concrete materials per W1044: cement, sand, gravel — quantities based on total concrete volume from steps 2/3; (b) Reinforcement steel per W986: rebar cutting and bending schedule; tie wire quantity; rebar chairs/spacers; (c) Waterproofing: for retaining walls — apply waterproofing membrane (cementitious or bituminous) to the back face (soil side) before backfilling; quantity based on wall area; (d) Backfill and drainage: gravel (¾&quot; crushed stone) for drainage layer behind wall; filter fabric (non-woven geotextile) to prevent soil clogging the drainage; perforated PVC drain pipe (110mm); (e) Compaction: gravel base compaction — manual tamper for small projects, plate compactor rental per W1094 for larger projects; (f) Tools: carpentry tools for formwork (hammer, saw, level, plumb bob, measuring tape, string line), concrete tools (wheelbarrow, shovel, trowel, vibrator rental per W1094), and rebar tools (bolt cutter or hacksaw, bending tool, tie wire twister)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1102_Task9" name="Estimate, Safety Advisory &amp; Professional Referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Estimate, Safety Advisory &amp; Professional Referral: (a) system generates itemized estimate with: structural sketch (simplified section view of retaining wall or formwork layout), complete BOM organized by category (structural, concrete, reinforcement, formwork, drainage, tools), quantities and prices, total estimated cost; (b) safety and engineering advisory: &quot;Retaining walls exceeding 1.0m height and all structural foundations must be designed by a licensed Civil Engineer. The National Structural Code of the Philippines (NSCP) 2015 governs structural design in Seismic Zone 4. This material estimation is for quantity purposes only and does not constitute a structural design. BuildRight Depot strongly recommends engaging a licensed Civil Engineer to design and supervise the construction of retaining walls and foundations.&quot;; (c) for retaining walls &gt; 3.0m: system requires a disclaimer that the estimation is for preliminary budgeting only and must not be used for construction without a professional engineer&#x27;s design; (d) system offers referral to licensed civil engineers and contractors per W904; (e) estimate saved to customer loyalty account
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1102_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1102_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1102_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1102_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: must not produce designs that appear to substitute for professional engineering
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1102_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1102_Annotation11" targetRef="W1102_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1102_Flow13" sourceRef="W1102_Start4" targetRef="W1102_Task5" />
