    <bpmn:process id="W_W1124" name="W1124. Customer Construction Material Compatibility Cross-Reference &amp; Substitution Advisory" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquiry about product compatibility, or system identifies out-of-stock item requiring substitution recommendation
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 compatibility queries/month across all stores (peak during summer renovation season Mar–May)
Volume: 1–5 product pairs per query
Owner: Sales Associate (Department-specific)
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Customer
Source: workflow W1124 — Customer Construction Material Compatibility Cross-Reference &amp; Substitution Advisory</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1124_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1124_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1124_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1124_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1124_Start4" name="Customer inquiry about product compatibility, or system identifies out-of-stock item…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1124_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1124_Task5" name="Customer Need Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Need Identification: (a) customer approaches sales associate with project description or product list; (b) sales associate identifies the project type: bathroom renovation, electrical installation, plumbing repair, roofing, painting, etc.; (c) determines customer skill level: professional contractor, experienced DIYer, or first-time DIYer; (d) captures key project parameters: room size, surface material, load requirements, environmental conditions (indoor/outdoor, wet/dry area)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1124_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1124_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1124_Task6" name="Compatibility Cross-Reference Lookup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Compatibility Cross-Reference Lookup: (a) sales associate scans or searches primary product in ERP mobile app or in-store kiosk; (b) system displays compatibility matrix: required complementary products (adhesive, primer, connector, fastener), compatible brands/models, and incompatibility warnings; (c) system highlights common mismatch errors (e.g., &quot;Using mastic adhesive with large-format porcelain tile — recommend modified thin-set mortar instead&quot;); (d) for electrical and plumbing: system applies Philippine building code requirements (National Structural Code of the Philippines, Philippine Electrical Code) to validate specifications; (e) if primary product is out-of-stock, system suggests verified substitutes per W279 with compatibility confirmation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1124_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1124_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1124_Task7" name="Customer Advisory &amp; Bundle Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer Advisory &amp; Bundle Recommendation: (a) sales associate presents compatibility-verified product selection to customer; (b) explains why certain combinations are required (e.g., &quot;This waterproofing membrane requires this specific primer for proper adhesion — using a different primer will void the manufacturer warranty&quot;); (c) offers complete bundle: all required complementary materials (adhesive, grout, spacers, waterproofing, tools) with bundle pricing per W910; (d) for complex projects (full bathroom renovation, electrical panel upgrade), recommends consultation with in-store design consultant (W148) or pro desk specialist (W112); (e) provides printed or emailed project material list with compatibility notes for future reference
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1124_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1124_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1124_Task8" name="Post-Sale Follow-Up &amp; Issue Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-Sale Follow-Up &amp; Issue Tracking: (a) system logs compatibility advisory as part of customer&#x27;s purchase history; (b) if customer returns with compatibility-related product failure (e.g., tile delamination due to wrong adhesive), the advisory record is referenced to determine if correct guidance was provided; (c) compatibility issues reported to merchandising team for product data improvement (W50 PIM); (d) recurring compatibility confusion flagged for better product labeling, shelf signage, or package bundling
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1124_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1124_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1124_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1124_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1124_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: recommendations
Owner: Sales Associate (Department-specific)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1124_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1124_Annotation10" targetRef="W1124_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1124_Flow12" sourceRef="W1124_Start4" targetRef="W1124_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1124_Flow13" sourceRef="W1124_Task5" targetRef="W1124_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1124_Flow14" sourceRef="W1124_Task6" targetRef="W1124_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1124_Flow15" sourceRef="W1124_Task7" targetRef="W1124_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1124_Flow16" sourceRef="W1124_Task8" targetRef="W1124_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1124_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1124_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1124">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1124_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1124_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1124_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1124_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1129" name="W1129. Customer Interior Design Material Board Curation &amp; Mood Board Assembly Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests design consultation for renovation project, or walks in with design inspiration (magazine photo, Pinterest board, contractor plan)
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 material board requests/month across all stores (peak during summer renovation season)
Volume: 1 material board per request (typically covers 1–2 rooms)
Owner: Sales Associate (Design-trained) / Design Consultant (W148)
Participants: Sales Associate / Design Consultant, Customer, Department Supervisors (relevant departments)
Source: workflow W1129 — Customer Interior Design Material Board Curation &amp; Mood Board Assembly Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1129_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1129_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1129_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1129_Start3" name="Customer requests design consultation for renovation project, or walks in with design…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1129_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1129_Task4" name="Customer Design Consultation &amp; Style Profiling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Design Consultation &amp; Style Profiling: (a) customer describes renovation project: room type (bathroom, kitchen, living room, bedroom), design style preference (modern minimalist, industrial, tropical Filipino, Mediterranean, Scandinavian), budget range, and existing elements to keep; (b) design-trained sales associate or design consultant reviews customer&#x27;s inspiration materials (photos, magazine clippings, phone images); (c) associate uses in-store design kiosk or tablet to browse BuildRight&#x27;s product catalog filtered by customer&#x27;s style, budget, and room type; (d) initial color palette established: 2–3 primary colors, 1–2 accent colors
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Design Consultant
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–25 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1129_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1129_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1129_Task5" name="Material Selection &amp; Sample Gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material Selection &amp; Sample Gathering: (a) associate guides customer through relevant departments to select physical samples: tiles (floor and wall) — 2–3 options per surface; paint — color swatches or mixed sample pots; countertop material (granite, quartz, laminate) — sample chips; cabinet hardware (handles, knobs) — physical samples; plumbing fixtures (faucet, shower head) — display models or catalog photos; lighting fixtures — catalog or display samples; (b) for each material, system shows: price per unit/sqm, availability, lead time, and complementary product suggestions; (c) customer selects preferred option for each material category; (d) associate gathers physical samples (tile chips, paint swatches, material chips)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Design Consultant
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 20–40 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1129_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1129_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1129_Task6" name="Material Board Assembly &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Board Assembly &amp; Documentation: (a) associate assembles physical material board on store-provided foam board (A3 size): tiles arranged as they would appear (floor tile at bottom, wall tile above, accent tile as border), paint swatches showing wall color and trim, countertop sample, hardware samples placed on countertop, fixture photos pinned alongside; (b) associate photographs completed material board for digital record; (c) system generates product list linked to material board: each item with SKU, quantity needed (based on room dimensions), unit price, and estimated total; (d) digital material board saved to customer&#x27;s account for future access and sharing with contractor
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Design Consultant
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1129_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1129_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1129_Task7" name="Quotation Generation &amp; Sales Conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quotation Generation &amp; Sales Conversion: (a) system calculates total project cost based on room dimensions and selected materials; (b) quotation generated per W542 with itemized material list and room-specific quantities; (c) bundle discount offered if customer purchases complete material board package: 5–10% off total vs. individual item pricing per W910; (d) if customer approves: sales order created with scheduled delivery or will-call per W773; (e) if customer takes material board home to decide: associate schedules 48-hour follow-up call per W744; (f) material board retained by customer as reference; physical samples returned per W903 loan policy if not purchased
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1129_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1129_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1129_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1129_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1129_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Sales Associate (Design-trained) / Design Consultant (W148) review and approval gate
Owner: Sales Associate (Design-trained) / Design Consultant (W148)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1129_Assoc10" sourceRef="W1129_Annotation9" targetRef="W1129_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
