    <bpmn:process id="W_W1138" name="W1138. Customer Construction Worker Safety Gear Bundle Recommendation &amp; Compliance Package" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases construction materials (especially for new projects), or inquires about PPE/safety equipment, or store identifies contractor/trade customer
Frequency: ~6,000–8,000 safety gear recommendations/month across all stores
Volume: 1 bundle recommendation per customer interaction
Owner: Sales Associate (Safety &amp; PPE Department)
Participants: Sales Associate, Customer (Contractor/Worker), Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1138 — Customer Construction Worker Safety Gear Bundle Recommendation &amp; Compliance Package</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1138_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1138_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1138_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1138_Start3" name="Customer purchases construction materials (especially for new projects), or inquires…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1138_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1138_Task4" name="Customer Identification &amp; Needs Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Identification &amp; Needs Assessment: (a) when customer purchases construction materials (cement, rebar, electrical supplies, plumbing materials), Sales Associate asks about project type and worker count; (b) for contractor/trade customers: &quot;How many workers will be on site? Do they have complete PPE?&quot;; (c) for DIY customers: &quot;Are you doing the work yourself? Here&#x27;s what you&#x27;ll need to stay safe&quot;; (d) identify worker roles: masonry, carpentry, electrical, plumbing, painting, welding, general labor, scaffolding; (e) assess current PPE condition: &quot;Do your workers already have hard hats and safety boots that are in good condition?&quot;
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1138_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1138_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1138_Task5" name="Bundle Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Bundle Recommendation: (a) Sales Associate recommends pre-configured safety bundle from ERP based on worker role: General Construction Pack (hard hat, safety glasses, dust mask N95, leather gloves, high-vis vest, steel-toed boots) — PHP 2,500–3,500; Mason&#x27;s Pack (add knee pads, rubber gloves, long rubber boots); Electrician&#x27;s Pack (add insulated gloves, voltage tester, arc-flash safety glasses); Welder&#x27;s Pack (add welding helmet, leather apron, welding gloves, ear plugs); Scaffolding/Heights Pack (add full-body safety harness, lanyard, safety helmet with chin strap); (b) system displays bundle with itemized contents and individual vs. bundle pricing (bundle discount: 10–15% vs. individual items); (c) if customer has partial PPE already: system recommends only missing items à la carte
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1138_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1138_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1138_Task6" name="Compliance Education &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance Education &amp; Documentation: (a) Sales Associate provides brief DOLE compliance overview: &quot;Under DOLE Department Order No. 13, all construction workers must wear hard hats, safety shoes, and appropriate PPE on site. Employers are responsible for providing PPE at no cost to workers&quot;; (b) offers DOLE compliance checklist printed or emailed from ERP; (c) for contractors: offers to generate a &quot;Safety Compliance Certificate&quot; — a BuildRight-branded document listing all PPE items purchased, which the contractor can present to DOLE inspectors or project owners as evidence of compliance; (d) certificates stored in customer&#x27;s account for annual renewal tracking
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1138_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1138_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1138_Task7" name="Sale Processing &amp; PPE Replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sale Processing &amp; PPE Replenishment: (a) PPE bundle added to customer&#x27;s transaction at POS with bundle pricing applied; (b) loyalty points earned on PPE purchases (standard 1 point per PHP 100); (c) system tracks PPE bundle sales by store and customer segment for inventory replenishment; (d) PPE items that are part of bundles monitored for stockout risk — safety items should not go out of stock (safety stock maintained at higher levels); (e) seasonal demand spikes: PPE demand increases during summer construction peak (Mar–May) and post-typhoon reconstruction (Jul–Dec)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / POS System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1138_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1138_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1138_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1138_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1138_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Sales Associate (Safety &amp; PPE Department)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1138_Assoc10" sourceRef="W1138_Annotation9" targetRef="W1138_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1138_Flow11" sourceRef="W1138_Start3" targetRef="W1138_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1138_Flow12" sourceRef="W1138_Task4" targetRef="W1138_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1138_Flow13" sourceRef="W1138_Task5" targetRef="W1138_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1138_Flow14" sourceRef="W1138_Task6" targetRef="W1138_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1138_Flow15" sourceRef="W1138_Task7" targetRef="W1138_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1138_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1138_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1138">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Start3_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Start3"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_End8_di" bpmnElement="W1138_End8"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1138_Annotation9_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Annotation9"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="290" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Flow11_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Flow11"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1138_Assoc10_di" bpmnElement="W1138_Assoc10"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1152" name="W1152. Store-Level Customer Project Material Quantity Verification &amp; Completeness Check" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer presents project material list for purchase, or customer requests verification that they have all required materials for their project
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 completeness checks/month across all stores (peak during summer renovation season)
Volume: 1 project material list per check (typically 15–60 line items)
Owner: Sales Associate (Department-specific)
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Customer
Source: workflow W1152 — Store-Level Customer Project Material Quantity Verification &amp; Completeness Check</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1152_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1152_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1152_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1152_Start3" name="Customer presents project material list for purchase, or customer requests verification…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1152_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1152_Task4" name="Project Type Identification &amp; Checklist Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Type Identification &amp; Checklist Selection: (a) customer presents material list (paper, phone photo, or BuildRight project list from W894 Project Vault); (b) sales associate identifies project type from list or customer description: bathroom renovation, kitchen renovation, electrical installation, plumbing repair, roofing, fencing, painting, flooring, or general construction; (c) system loads corresponding completeness checklist: e.g., &quot;Bathroom Renovation&quot; checklist includes 47 required items across 8 categories (structural, waterproofing, plumbing, electrical, tiles, fixtures, hardware, consumables); (d) if project type unclear, associate uses guided questionnaire: &quot;What room are you working on?&quot;, &quot;Is it a new installation or renovation?&quot;, &quot;What&#x27;s the approximate area?&quot;
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1152_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1152_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1152_Task5" name="Material List Cross-Reference &amp; Gap Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material List Cross-Reference &amp; Gap Identification: (a) associate scans or enters customer&#x27;s material list into ERP completeness checker; (b) system compares customer&#x27;s list against completeness checklist: matched items (customer has it), missing required items (customer needs it), missing recommended items (customer should consider it), quantity check (is the quantity sufficient for the project scope based on area/dimensions?); (c) system flags gaps: &quot;You&#x27;re tiling a 15 sqm bathroom floor — your list has 14 sqm of tiles. We recommend purchasing 10% extra for cuts and breakage. Add 2 sqm?&quot;; &quot;You have PVC pipes and fittings but no PVC solvent cement. Required for installation.&quot;; &quot;You selected a shower faucet but no shower head. Do you need one?&quot;; (d) for compatibility: system also runs compatibility check per W1124 to verify selected items work together
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1152_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1152_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1152_Task6" name="Customer Review &amp; Gap Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer Review &amp; Gap Resolution: (a) associate presents completeness check results on tablet or printout: ✓ items already on list, ⚠ missing required items, 💡 recommended additions; (b) for missing required items: associate explains why the item is needed and offers to add to purchase; (c) for quantity shortfalls: associate explains the calculation (e.g., &quot;Based on your 20 sqm floor area with 10% waste factor, you need 22 sqm of tiles. Your list has 18 sqm — that&#x27;s 4 sqm short.&quot;); (d) customer decides which gaps to fill; (e) associate adds approved items to the sales order; (f) system generates updated material list with all items (original + additions) and total estimated project cost
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1152_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1152_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1152_Task7" name="Post-Purchase Project List Archival">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-Purchase Project List Archival: (a) completed material list saved to customer&#x27;s account as a &quot;Verified Project List&quot; per W894 (Project Vault); (b) customer can share verified list with contractor or reference for future similar projects; (c) system generates project receipt: items purchased, quantities, prices, and BuildRight store location(s); (d) if customer returns within 30 days for missing items from the same project: associate can pull up verified list and quickly identify and add missing items; (e) completeness check data feeds analytics: most commonly missed items by project type → used to improve checklist and staff training
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1152_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1152_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1152_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1152_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1152_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Sales Associate (Department-specific) review and approval gate
Owner: Sales Associate (Department-specific)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1152_Assoc10" sourceRef="W1152_Annotation9" targetRef="W1152_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1152_Flow11" sourceRef="W1152_Start3" targetRef="W1152_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1152_Flow12" sourceRef="W1152_Task4" targetRef="W1152_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1152_Flow13" sourceRef="W1152_Task5" targetRef="W1152_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1152_Flow14" sourceRef="W1152_Task6" targetRef="W1152_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1152_Flow15" sourceRef="W1152_Task7" targetRef="W1152_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1152_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1152_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1152">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1152_Start3_di" bpmnElement="W1152_Start3"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
