    <bpmn:process id="W_W1154" name="W1154. Store-Level Customer Paint VOC &amp; Indoor Air Quality Compliance Advisory" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases paint or coating products, or customer inquires about indoor air quality, or customer specifies enclosed-space application
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 VOC advisory interactions/month across all stores (paint is 8% of active SKUs, ~2,800 SKUs)
Volume: 1–5 paint/coating products per interaction
Owner: Sales Associate (Paint &amp; Finishes Department)
Participants: Sales Associate, Customer
Source: workflow W1154 — Store-Level Customer Paint VOC &amp; Indoor Air Quality Compliance Advisory</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1154_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1154_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1154_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1154_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1154_Start4" name="Customer purchases paint or coating products, or customer inquires about indoor air…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1154_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1154_Task5" name="Application Environment Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Application Environment Assessment: (a) customer approaches paint department or system identifies paint purchase at POS; (b) sales associate asks application questions: &quot;Where will this paint be used?&quot; (bedroom, bathroom, kitchen, living room, exterior, commercial space), &quot;How large is the space?&quot;, &quot;Is the space well-ventilated?&quot;, &quot;Are there children, elderly, pregnant women, or anyone with respiratory conditions in the household?&quot;, &quot;Is this for a BERDE/LEED-certified building project?&quot;; (c) associate enters responses into ERP paint advisory module
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1154_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1154_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1154_Task6" name="VOC Level Matching &amp; Product Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VOC Level Matching &amp; Product Recommendation: (a) system displays paint options filtered by application: enclosed rooms with vulnerable occupants → recommend zero-VOC or low-VOC only; well-ventilated spaces without vulnerable occupants → low or medium VOC acceptable; exterior applications → no VOC restriction (outdoor ventilation sufficient); commercial/industrial with PPE → all options available; BERDE/LEED projects → zero or low-VOC with compliance documentation; (b) system shows VOC content (g/L) for each paint option alongside standard performance specs (coverage, durability, finish); (c) associate explains trade-offs: zero/low-VOC paints may have slightly fewer color options or longer drying time but are safer for indoor use; (d) for high-VOC products selected for enclosed spaces: system displays advisory warning and requires customer acknowledgment per W520-style prompt
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1154_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1154_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1154_Task7" name="Ventilation &amp; Safety Guidance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ventilation &amp; Safety Guidance: (a) for any indoor paint purchase, associate provides ventilation guidance: &quot;Open windows and use fans during and after painting&quot;, &quot;Wait at least 24 hours before reoccupying the room for low-VOC; 48–72 hours for medium/high-VOC&quot;, &quot;Wear a paint mask (N95 or VOC-rated) when applying solvent-based paints&quot;; (b) system suggests complementary safety products: paint mask (N95), gloves, drop cloths, painter&#x27;s tape, ventilation fan; (c) for large indoor projects: recommend purchasing or renting a portable ventilation fan per W139 (tool rental); (d) guidance printed on receipt alongside paint mixing instructions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1154_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1154_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1154_Task8" name="Compliance Documentation (BERDE/LEED)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Compliance Documentation (BERDE/LEED): (a) for customers specifying green building certification: system generates VOC compliance certificate for each paint product showing: product name, manufacturer, VOC content (g/L), applicable standard (DENR DAO, Green Seal, or equivalent), and batch number; (b) certificate available as PDF for customer&#x27;s LEED/BERDE documentation submission; (c) VOC compliance data maintained in product master and linked to SDS (W698)
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (if applicable)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1154_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1154_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1154_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1154_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1154_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Sales Associate (Paint &amp; Finishes Department)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1154_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1154_Annotation10" targetRef="W1154_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1154_Flow12" sourceRef="W1154_Start4" targetRef="W1154_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1154_Flow13" sourceRef="W1154_Task5" targetRef="W1154_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1154_Flow14" sourceRef="W1154_Task6" targetRef="W1154_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1154_Flow15" sourceRef="W1154_Task7" targetRef="W1154_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1154_Flow16" sourceRef="W1154_Task8" targetRef="W1154_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1154_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1154_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1154">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1154_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1154_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
