    <bpmn:process id="W_W1238" name="W1238. Customer Building Plan Review, Material Take-Off &amp; Professional Estimation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (typically contractor, builder, or homeowner with building permit) presents building plan/blueprint for material estimation
Frequency: ~5–10 plan reviews per store per month; ~1,000–2,000/month chain-wide
Volume: 200 stores × ~7 plans/month = ~1,400/month
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate, Category Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W1238 — Customer Building Plan Review, Material Take-Off &amp; Professional Estimation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1238_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1238_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1238_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1238_Start3" name="Customer (typically contractor, builder, or homeowner with building permit) presents…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1238_Task4" name="Plan intake &amp; scope assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Plan intake &amp; scope assessment: Customer presents building plan (blueprint, PDF, or sketch): (a) Department Supervisor reviews plan for scope (single-storey, multi-storey, residential, commercial); (b) identify which trades are covered (structural, architectural, plumbing, electrical); (c) confirm which materials customer wants from BuildRight vs. other sources
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1238_Task5" name="Structural material take-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Structural material take-off: For structural components: (a) foundation: estimate concrete volume (length × width × depth) → cement bags, sand, gravel; (b) hollow block walls: calculate wall area (less openings) ÷ block face area = blocks needed + wastage; (c) rebar: from structural plan — bar sizes, lengths, quantities per schedule; (d) formwork lumber: from floor area and number of pours
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1238_Task6" name="Architectural material take-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Architectural material take-off: (a) roofing: roof area from plan → roofing sheets + ridge caps + fasteners; (b) tiles (if in plan): floor area per room per W1227; (c) doors and windows: count from plan, sizes from schedule; (d) paint: wall/ceiling area × coats ÷ coverage per gallon
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1238_Task7" name="Plumbing &amp; electrical estimation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Plumbing &amp; electrical estimation: (a) plumbing: pipe lengths from layout + fittings count + fixtures per W1227; (b) electrical: wire lengths from layout + switches/outlets count + panel/breakers from load schedule
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1238_Task8" name="Consolidated material list &amp; quote">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consolidated material list &amp; quote: (a) compile all materials into single list organized by trade; (b) assign BuildRight SKUs to each material; (c) apply quantities with wastage factors (cement +5%, tiles +10%, lumber +15%); (d) generate quote with trade pricing per W112 if contractor has trade account; (e) calculate total project material cost
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1238_Task9" name="Customer review &amp; order conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer review &amp; order conversion: (a) review material list with customer; (b) adjust quantities or swap products; (c) discuss phased delivery schedule (foundation first, then structural, then architectural); (d) convert to project order per W58 with staged call-off per W164; (e) set up project billing per W165 if applicable
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Customer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1238_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1238_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1238_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1238_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1238_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1238_Annotation11" targetRef="W1238_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow13" sourceRef="W1238_Start3" targetRef="W1238_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow14" sourceRef="W1238_Task4" targetRef="W1238_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow15" sourceRef="W1238_Task5" targetRef="W1238_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow16" sourceRef="W1238_Task6" targetRef="W1238_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow17" sourceRef="W1238_Task7" targetRef="W1238_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow18" sourceRef="W1238_Task8" targetRef="W1238_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1238_Flow19" sourceRef="W1238_Task9" targetRef="W1238_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1238_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1238_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1238">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Start3_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Start3"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_End10_di" bpmnElement="W1238_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1680" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1238_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="290" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1450" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1630" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1680" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1238_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W1238_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1246" name="W1246. Store-Level Customer Roofing &amp; Structural Material Load Calculation &amp; Estimation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests roofing or structural material estimation for a construction project
Frequency: ~10–20 roofing estimations per store per month; ~2,000–4,000/month chain-wide
Volume: 200 stores × ~15 estimations/month = ~3,000/month
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate, Customer
Source: workflow W1246 — Store-Level Customer Roofing &amp; Structural Material Load Calculation &amp; Estimation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1246_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1246_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1246_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1246_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1246_Start4" name="Customer requests roofing or structural material estimation for a construction project">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1246_Task5" name="Project parameters capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project parameters capture: Sales Associate captures roofing parameters from customer: (a) building footprint (length × width); (b) roof type (gable, hip, combination); (c) roof pitch/rise (Philippine standard: 30–45 degrees for typhoon country); (d) overhang width (typically 0.6–1.0m); (e) preferred roofing material (GI sheet gauge, roof tile type)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1246_Task6" name="Roof area calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Roof area calculation: Department Supervisor calculates: (a) roof slope length: (rise² + run²)^0.5 per pitch; (b) roof plane area: slope length × building length (+ overhang on both sides); (c) total roof area: sum of all planes (2 for gable, 4 for hip); (d) applicable waste factor: +5% for simple gable, +10–15% for hip/complex with valleys
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1246_Task7" name="Material quantity calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material quantity calculation: (a) roofing sheets: total roof area ÷ effective coverage per sheet (net after overlap); (b) ridge caps: ridge length ÷ coverage per ridge cap piece; (c) C-purlins (for steel frame): roof slope length ÷ purlin spacing (typically 0.6–0.8m) × number of planes; (d) truss material: calculated from span and spacing per structural design; (e) fasteners: roofing nails/tek screws per sheet × number of sheets; (f) insulation (if applicable): same area as roofing
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1246_Task8" name="Quote generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quote generation: (a) assign BuildRight SKUs to each material item; (b) apply quantities with wastage; (c) calculate line totals at trade pricing per W112 if applicable; (d) generate project quote with delivery estimate for bulky items
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1246_Task9" name="Customer review &amp; sale">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer review &amp; sale: (a) review material list with customer; (b) discuss delivery options (roofing sheets and C-purlins are too large for customer vehicle); (c) convert to sale or save quote; (d) arrange delivery per W19 or W6
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Customer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1246_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1246_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1246_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
