    <bpmn:process id="W_W1284" name="W1284. Customer Bulk Material Quantity Takeoff &amp; Quotation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (typically contractor, builder, or homeowner) requests material estimate for a construction project based on building plans or verbal description
Frequency: ~40–60 quantity takeoff requests per store per month; ~8,000–12,000 chain-wide
Volume: Average takeoff covers ~15–40 material line items; ~5–10% conversion to full project order per W112
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate, Customer, Category Manager (for large projects)
Source: workflow W1284 — Customer Bulk Material Quantity Takeoff &amp; Quotation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1284_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1284_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1284_Lane2" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1284_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1284_Start4" name="Customer (typically contractor, builder, or homeowner) requests material estimate for a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1284_Task5" name="Customer intake &amp; project scope">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer intake &amp; project scope: Department Supervisor receives customer&#x27;s request: (a) review building plans, sketches, or photos customer provides, (b) if no plans: conduct structured interview — what are you building? (house extension, bathroom renovation, fence, etc.), dimensions, number of floors, materials preference, (c) determine project type: new construction, renovation, repair; (d) estimate project size to allocate appropriate time (small: &lt;30 min, medium: 30–60 min, large: schedule appointment)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1284_Task6" name="Material quantity calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material quantity calculation: Department Supervisor performs quantity takeoff based on project scope: (a) structural: cement bags = floor area × 0.4 bags/sqm (typical); hollow blocks = wall area ÷ 0.08 sqm/block (= area × ~12.5 blocks/sqm, standard 8&quot;×16&quot;); rebar = based on structural requirement (customer to verify with engineer); sand/gravel = cement bags × 0.05 cu.m. per bag ratio; (b) finishes: tiles = floor/wall area × 1.10 (10% wastage); paint = area ÷ 25 sqm per gallon (2 coats) × 1.15 wastage; (c) plumbing: pipe length from plan, fittings estimated per connection type; (d) electrical: wire length from plan + 15%, switches/outlets counted from plan; (e) hardware: nails, screws, cement nails, adhesive based on project type
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1284_Task7" name="SKU matching &amp; availability check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: SKU matching &amp; availability check: Department Supervisor maps calculated quantities to BuildRight SKUs: (a) select appropriate product grade/brand based on customer budget preference (economy vs. premium), (b) system checks real-time availability at store and nearest DC for each item, (c) identify out-of-stock items and propose alternatives, (d) note lead times for items requiring special order per W38
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1284_Task8" name="Quotation generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quotation generation: (a) apply appropriate pricing: SRP for walk-in, trade price per W112 for registered trade accounts, corporate pricing for registered B2B per W24, (b) calculate delivery logistics: bulk items (cement, sand, gravel) require delivery scheduling per W1283 or W6, (c) generate project quotation in system with: item list, quantities, unit prices, line totals, delivery estimate, quotation validity (30 days), (d) print or email quotation to customer
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1284_Task9" name="Quotation review with customer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation review with customer: Department Supervisor reviews quotation with customer: (a) walk through each material category, explain quantities and assumptions, (b) highlight items that may need adjustment based on actual site conditions, (c) discuss delivery options and logistics for bulky materials, (d) discuss optional items not in takeoff (tools, PPE, adhesives, finishing materials), (e) note any substitutions customer requests
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1284_Task10" name="Follow-up &amp; conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Follow-up &amp; conversion: (a) for trade/corporate accounts: Sales Associate follows up within 7 days per CRM workflow, (b) system tracks quotation status (draft → sent → viewed → accepted → expired), (c) if customer accepts: convert quotation to sales order (full project) or partial order (phased delivery), (d) for large projects (&gt;PHP 500K): escalate to Category Manager for project pricing negotiation and dedicated logistics coordination per W112
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min/follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1284_Task11" name="Post-project feedback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-project feedback: For completed projects, Department Supervisor follows up: (a) were material quantities accurate? (too much = waste for customer; too little = return trip = poor experience), (b) capture actual quantities used vs. estimated for takeoff accuracy improvement, (c) request customer review/testimonial for marketing per W14, (d) identify follow-on project opportunities (extension, finish-out, landscaping)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1284_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1284_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1284_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1284_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: requiring trade account registration for detailed takeoffs or charging a refundable consultation fee for non-members
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1284_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1284_Annotation13" targetRef="W1284_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1284_Flow15" sourceRef="W1284_Start4" targetRef="W1284_Task5" />
