    <bpmn:process id="W_W1314" name="W1314. Customer Project Material List (Bill of Materials) Creation, Management &amp; Reorder Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests a comprehensive material list for a home construction or renovation project; or contractor/building professional requests project BOM for bidding
Frequency: ~30–50 project BOM requests per store per month; ~6,000–10,000/month chain-wide
Volume: ~200 stores × ~40 BOMs/month = ~8,000 BOMs/month; average BOM: 15–40 line items covering 3–8 product categories
Owner: Department Supervisor (Trade Counter / Pro Desk)
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter), Department Supervisor, Customer, Category Manager (for pricing), Supply Planning Analyst (for availability)
Source: workflow W1314 — Customer Project Material List (Bill of Materials) Creation, Management &amp; Reorder Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1314_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1314_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1314_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1314_Start3" name="Customer requests a comprehensive material list for a home construction or renovation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1314_Task4" name="Customer project scoping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer project scoping: (a) Sales Associate interviews customer about the project: (i) project type (new construction, renovation, extension, fit-out), (ii) project scope (square meters, number of rooms/floors, specific rooms), (iii) budget range, (iv) timeline (when does construction start? target completion?), (v) customer type: DIY homeowner, contractor with crew, or builder/developer; (b) based on project scope, Sales Associate selects appropriate BOM template from system: (i) standard house construction BOM (1-story, 50–100 sqm), (ii) bathroom renovation BOM (5–10 sqm), (iii) kitchen renovation BOM (8–15 sqm), (iv) fence construction BOM (per linear meter), (v) custom BOM (no template — built from scratch); (c) Sales Associate uses the BOM template as a starting point and customizes per customer&#x27;s specific requirements: product preferences (brand, grade, color), specification changes, additions, and omissions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1314_Task5" name="BOM creation with quantity calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BOM creation with quantity calculation: (a) Sales Associate builds the BOM line by line in the ERP BOM module: (i) select product category → select specific item → enter quantity, (ii) system calculates quantity based on project dimensions: e.g., for a 10 sqm bathroom floor tile at 60cm × 60cm tile size: 10 sqm ÷ 0.36 sqm/tile = 28 tiles + 10% wastage = 31 tiles; e.g., for a 50 sqm house floor screed: cement bags = area × 0.12 bags/sqm (thin screed; a full slab uses ~0.4 bags/sqm per W1284) = 6 bags + 15% wastage = 7 bags; (iii) for each line item, system displays: product description, SKU, specification, unit of measure, unit price (SRP), quantity, and line total; (b) system suggests complementary items: (i) if customer selects tiles: suggest tile adhesive, grout, spacers, and tile cutter rental (W139), (ii) if customer selects paint: suggest primer, rollers, brushes, drop cloths, and paint mixing (W168), (iii) if customer selects plumbing fixtures: suggest pipes, fittings, sealant, and tools; (c) Sales Associate reviews with customer and adjusts as needed; (d) system calculates BOM total: subtotal (SRP), project discount (if applicable — typically 5–15% for full BOM purchase), VAT (12%), and grand total
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1314_Task6" name="BOM availability check &amp; pricing confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: BOM availability check &amp; pricing confirmation: (a) system checks real-time inventory availability for all BOM items at the customer&#x27;s preferred store: (i) items in stock: confirmed available, (ii) items low stock (&lt; 5 units): flagged — may sell out before customer purchase, recommend reservation per W546, (iii) items out of stock: system checks nearest store or DC availability — offer transfer (W219) or special order (W38), (iv) items not carried (special specifications): offer special order per W38 with lead time estimate; (b) for trade account customers: system applies trade pricing per W8 (5–15% discount based on account tier); (c) for project-level pricing (BOM total &gt; PHP 50,000): Department Supervisor reviews and may offer additional project discount: (i) PHP 50K–100K: additional 3–5% project discount, (ii) PHP 100K–500K: additional 5–8% project discount, (iii) &gt; PHP 500K: VP Merchandising approval required for pricing exception; (d) finalized BOM saved in customer&#x27;s profile with project name and reference number
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1314_Task7" name="BOM delivery scheduling &amp; fulfillment coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BOM delivery scheduling &amp; fulfillment coordination: (a) for customers purchasing the full BOM: (i) Sales Associate coordinates delivery scheduling: large projects may require 3–5 scheduled deliveries (foundation materials first, then framing, then finishing), (ii) system creates delivery schedule with dates, items, and quantities per delivery, (iii) for trade accounts: schedule billed deliveries per credit terms; (b) for BOMs exceeding PHP 100K: Department Supervisor assigns the BOM a dedicated project coordinator (rotated among Sales Associates) for follow-up and reorder management; (c) system generates project BOM summary for customer: itemized list with pricing, delivery schedule, and trade account terms (if applicable)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1314_Task8" name="BOM reorder tracking &amp; project completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: BOM reorder tracking &amp; project completion: (a) as the customer&#x27;s project progresses: (i) customer returns to BuildRight for additional materials not in original BOM (e.g., changed design, additional scope), (ii) Sales Associate retrieves original BOM from customer profile, adds additional items, tracks project spend against original BOM, (iii) system tracks BOM fulfillment rate: % of BOM items purchased vs. planned — identifies customers who started but haven&#x27;t completed their BOM purchase (follow-up opportunity); (b) monthly: Department Supervisor reviews open BOMs: (i) BOMs with no purchase activity in 30 days: Sales Associate contacts customer for follow-up — is the project still proceeding? does the customer need any modifications?, (ii) BOMs with partial fulfillment: encourage customer to complete remaining items with targeted promotion or delivery incentive; (c) upon project completion: Sales Associate marks BOM as completed, records total actual purchase vs. original BOM estimate (variance analysis feeds demand planning accuracy for W31)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Monthly review: 2–3 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1314_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1314_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1314_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1314_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Trade Counter / Pro Desk) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Trade Counter / Pro Desk)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1314_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1314_Annotation10" targetRef="W1314_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1314_Flow12" sourceRef="W1314_Start3" targetRef="W1314_Task4" />
