    <bpmn:process id="W_W1491" name="W1491. Customer Kitchen &amp; Bathroom Design Consultation, 3D Rendering &amp; Material Take-Off Generation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests kitchen or bathroom renovation design consultation at store service counter or via online booking
Frequency: ~8–15 consultations per store per month; higher in stores near residential development areas
Volume: ~1,600–3,000 consultations/month chain-wide; ~40–60% conversion rate to material purchase
Owner: Project Estimator
Participants: Customer, Project Estimator, Department Supervisor (Plumbing &amp; Electrical), Installation Coordinator
Source: workflow W1491 — Customer Kitchen &amp; Bathroom Design Consultation, 3D Rendering &amp; Material Take-Off Generation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1491_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1491_Lane1" name="Project Estimator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1491_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1491_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1491_Start4" name="Customer requests kitchen or bathroom renovation design consultation at store service…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1491_Task5" name="Consultation intake &amp; measurement gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Consultation intake &amp; measurement gathering: (a) Project Estimator meets customer at the design consultation station (dedicated area with large screen, product samples, and tile/fixture catalogs); (b) captures project scope: kitchen or bathroom, room dimensions (customer provides measurements or schedules a site visit per PA-12.1), budget range, style preferences (modern, minimalist, industrial, Filipino-Spanish), and timeline; (c) if customer has photos of current space: uploads to system for reference; (d) if no measurements: schedules site measurement visit (separate workflow per W1491 extension)
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1491_Task6" name="Product selection &amp; design layout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product selection &amp; design layout: (a) using the room dimensions and customer preferences, Project Estimator guides customer through product selection on the 3D design tool: (i) floor and wall tiles: selection from BuildRight&#x27;s tile catalog with quantity calculator based on floor/wall area + 10% waste factor; (ii) fixtures: toilet, faucet, shower system, sink from display catalog; (iii) cabinetry: modular cabinet system dimensions and finishes; (iv) countertops: granite, quartz, or laminate options with pricing per square meter; (v) plumbing fittings: visible and concealed components; (vi) electrical: lighting fixtures, outlets, switches; (b) Project Estimator enters selections into 3D design tool and generates real-time cost estimate; (c) customer adjusts selections to fit budget; (d) design iterations until customer approves layout
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 45–90 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1491_Task7" name="3D rendering generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: 3D rendering generation: (a) system generates photorealistic 3D rendering of the designed space using selected products and materials; (b) multiple views: overhead plan, perspective views from 2–3 angles, close-up detail views; (c) rendering includes realistic lighting, textures, and product-specific appearances (e.g., exact tile pattern from catalog); (d) customer reviews rendering on large screen; (e) minor adjustments made if needed; (f) final rendering exported as PDF and emailed to customer along with a shareable web link valid for 30 days
Responsible (R): System / Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min (automated rendering)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1491_Task8" name="Material take-off (MTO) generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Material take-off (MTO) generation: (a) system auto-generates complete MTO from the approved design: (i) all selected products with exact SKU, quantity, and unit price; (ii) computed quantities for tiles (area-based), grout, adhesive, and waterproofing; (iii) plumbing materials: pipes, fittings, valves, connectors based on room layout; (iv) electrical materials: wire length estimate, conduit, junction boxes based on fixture placement; (v) consumables: sealant, screws, anchors, cement; (b) MTO totals displayed with: material cost subtotal, estimated installation labor cost (if BuildRight installation selected per PA-12.1), delivery fee estimate per W1488; (c) Project Estimator reviews MTO for completeness and adjusts quantities for waste factors
Responsible (R): System / Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1491_Task9" name="Quotation generation &amp; customer follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quotation generation &amp; customer follow-up: (a) system generates formal quotation document with: 3D renderings, itemized MTO, pricing, validity period (30 days), terms and conditions; (b) quotation saved in customer&#x27;s profile in CRM; (c) Project Estimator schedules follow-up call/email at 7 days and 14 days if customer does not proceed; (d) if customer proceeds: quotation converted to sales order per PA-11.2 project sales workflow; (e) installation scheduled per PA-12.1 if BuildRight installation selected; (f) material delivery coordinated per W1488 or customer pickup
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min + follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1491_Task10" name="Design library &amp; reuse">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Design library &amp; reuse: (a) completed designs saved to store design library (anonymized if customer declines data storage); (b) popular designs tagged by category and price range for future customer inspiration; (c) monthly: Department Supervisor reviews design conversion rates and popular product combinations to inform assortment decisions per PA-01.1
Responsible (R): Project Estimator / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1491_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1491_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1491_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1491_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: Project Estimator review and approval gate
Owner: Project Estimator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1491_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1491_Annotation12" targetRef="W1491_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow14" sourceRef="W1491_Start4" targetRef="W1491_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow15" sourceRef="W1491_Task5" targetRef="W1491_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow16" sourceRef="W1491_Task6" targetRef="W1491_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow17" sourceRef="W1491_Task7" targetRef="W1491_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow18" sourceRef="W1491_Task8" targetRef="W1491_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow19" sourceRef="W1491_Task9" targetRef="W1491_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1491_Flow20" sourceRef="W1491_Task10" targetRef="W1491_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1491_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1491_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1491">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1491_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1491_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
