    <bpmn:process id="W_W1517" name="W1517. Customer Structural Steel &amp; Rebar Estimation, Span Calculation &amp; Engineering Advisory Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests structural steel/rebar estimation for residential or small commercial construction (2–5 story building, floor area 50–500 sqm)
Frequency: ~80–120 consultations/month across 200 stores
Volume: Estimated material value: PHP 50K–500K per consultation
Owner: Project Estimator (Structural)
Participants: Project Estimator, Customer, Category Manager (Steel), licensed Structural Engineer (external consultant on retainer)
Source: workflow W1517 — Customer Structural Steel &amp; Rebar Estimation, Span Calculation &amp; Engineering Advisory Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1517_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1517_Lane1" name="Project Estimator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1517_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1517_Start3" name="Customer requests structural steel/rebar estimation for residential or small commercial…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1517_Task4" name="Customer intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer intake: (a) customer presents floor plan, building permit drawings, or rough sketch of structure; (b) Project Estimator captures: number of floors, floor area per floor, column spacing, beam spans, slab thickness, and intended use (residential, commercial); (c) if customer has structural plans from a licensed engineer: proceed to material takeoff (Step 4); if no structural plans: advise customer that structural design requires a licensed engineer per the Civil Engineering Law (RA 544) and PD 1096/NSCP
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1517_Task5" name="Span and load assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Span and load assessment (advisory only, not structural design): (a) using the store&#x27;s structural estimation reference tool (pre-programmed with NSCP-derived rules of thumb for typical Philippine residential construction): (i) estimate approximate column rebar requirements (number and diameter of main bars + ties based on column cross-section and floor count), (ii) estimate approximate beam rebar (main bars + stirrups based on span length), (iii) estimate slab reinforcement (welded wire mesh or rebar grid based on slab area and thickness), (iv) estimate structural steel members if applicable (I-beam/W-section sizes for spans &gt; 6m); (b) system generates approximate material list with quantities
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1517_Task6" name="Engineering referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Engineering referral (if required): (a) if project exceeds advisory scope (building &gt; 3 stories, commercial occupancy, unusual spans, seismic zone 4 per PHIVOLCS map): (i) Project Estimator refers customer to licensed Structural Engineer from BuildRight&#x27;s referral directory (per W1521 Contractor Referral); (ii) provides customer with BuildRight&#x27;s structural materials catalog and pricing for engineer reference; (b) if project is within scope (typical 1–2 story residential, standard spans): proceed to material takeoff
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1517_Task7" name="Material takeoff and quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Material takeoff and quotation: (a) system generates detailed material list: (i) rebar by diameter (10mm, 12mm, 16mm, 20mm, 25mm) × length (6m or 9m standard), quantities in pieces, computed weight in kg, (ii) tie wire (kg), (iii) welded wire mesh (sheets), (iv) structural steel sections (I-beam, C-purlin, angle bar) if applicable, (v) accessories (rebar chairs, spacers, chairs); (b) system checks current pricing from steel master and applies current market rate (steel prices fluctuate weekly in Philippines); (c) system checks stock availability at store and nearest DC
Responsible (R): Project Estimator / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1517_Task8" name="Customer consultation and order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer consultation and order: (a) Project Estimator presents material list, cost estimate, and availability to customer; (b) advises on: (i) order timing — steel prices may change if order is delayed, (ii) delivery logistics — rebar and steel are heavy/bulky items requiring truck delivery per W1509, (iii) cut-to-size options — store can cut rebar to specified lengths per W169 (Lumber &amp; Board Cutting adapted for steel); (c) customer decides: (i) purchase full quantity now, (ii) phased purchase aligned with construction schedule per W993 (Phased Material Delivery), (iii) take quotation for later
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1517_Task9" name="Post-sale follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-sale follow-up (for phased purchases): (a) system creates material schedule linked to customer project; (b) Project Estimator calls customer at scheduled phase milestones to confirm next delivery; (c) any design changes (customer&#x27;s engineer modifies structural plan) trigger re-estimation
Responsible (R): Project Estimator / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager (Steel)
Duration: 5–10 min/follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1517_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1517_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1517_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1517_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: mandatory engineering referral for projects exceeding advisory scope; operational: engineering referral for projects exceeding advisory scope
Owner: Project Estimator (Structural)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1517_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1517_Annotation11" targetRef="W1517_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
