    <bpmn:process id="W_W1518" name="W1518. Customer Solar PV System Sizing, ROI Modeling, Net Metering Application &amp; Installation Package Advisory" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquires about solar panel system for residential or small commercial property
Frequency: ~60–100 consultations/month across 200 stores (growing 30–40% year-over-year as solar adoption accelerates in Philippines)
Volume: Average system: 3–10 kWp; material value PHP 80K–400K; average ticket PHP 150K
Owner: Project Estimator (Electrical)
Participants: Project Estimator, Customer, Category Manager (Electrical), Solar Installation Partner (external)
Source: workflow W1518 — Customer Solar PV System Sizing, ROI Modeling, Net Metering Application &amp; Installation Package Advisory</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1518_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1518_Lane1" name="Project Estimator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1518_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1518_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1518_Start4" name="Customer inquires about solar panel system for residential or small commercial property">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1518_Task5" name="Customer intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer intake: (a) Project Estimator captures: (i) monthly electricity bill amount (PHP) and kWh consumption from utility bill, (ii) roof type (tin/GI sheet, concrete slab), (iii) approximate roof area available, (iv) roof orientation (N/S/E/W facing), (v) property type (residential, commercial), (vi) customer objective: maximize savings vs. backup power vs. grid independence; (b) if customer has photos of roof and meter: upload to system
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1518_Task6" name="System sizing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System sizing: (a) using BuildRight&#x27;s solar sizing tool: (i) input monthly kWh consumption → system calculates recommended kWp size (target: offset 60–80% of consumption for optimal ROI), (ii) system checks roof area feasibility (kWp → number of panels → sqm required at ~6–7 sqm/kWp for standard panels), (iii) adjusts for orientation loss: south-facing optimal (100%), east/west (80–85%), north (60–70%), (iv) adjusts for shading if customer reports obstructions; (b) system recommends: (i) solar panel model and quantity (from BuildRight stock), (ii) inverter size and type (string vs. microinverter), (iii) battery storage size (if backup power objective: lithium battery kWh; grid-tied without battery is standard for ROI optimization), (iv) mounting system (roof-mount rails, clamps, flashings), (v) balance-of-system components (DC/AC cabling, disconnects, surge protection, monitoring system)
Responsible (R): Project Estimator / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1518_Task7" name="ROI modeling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: ROI modeling: (a) system calculates: (i) estimated annual energy production (kWh/year based on location-specific solar irradiation data from PAG-ASA/PVGIS), (ii) estimated monthly savings (kWh × local utility rate), (iii) net metering credits for excess production exported to grid (per ERC net metering rules), (iv) total system cost (materials + installation partner fee), (v) payback period (years to break even), (vi) 25-year total savings projection; (b) system generates customer-facing ROI summary: payback period, monthly savings, 25-year net savings, CO₂ offset
Responsible (R): System / Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1518_Task8" name="Net metering application guidance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Net metering application guidance: (a) Project Estimator explains net metering process to customer: (i) customer applies to local distribution utility (DU) using ERC-prescribed forms, (ii) DU conducts technical review and interconnection agreement, (iii) DU installs bidirectional meter replacing existing unidirectional meter, (iv) process takes 30–90 days depending on DU; (b) provides BuildRight&#x27;s net metering application guide (standardized packet with: ERC application form template, sample single-line diagram, electrical design specification, and BuildRight system specification sheet); (c) advises customer to engage licensed Electrical Engineer or Master Electrician for net metering application — can refer from BuildRight&#x27;s contractor directory per W1521
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1518_Task9" name="Material quotation and order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Material quotation and order: (a) system generates material quotation: itemized list of all components, quantities, unit prices, total; (b) checks stock availability at store and DC; (c) presents installation partner options (if customer wants turnkey): 2–3 accredited solar installers from BuildRight&#x27;s contractor directory with estimated installation cost; (d) customer decides: (i) materials only (DIY or own electrician), (ii) materials + BuildRight installation partner; (e) if ordered: system creates sales order with scheduled delivery (solar panels require careful handling — no stacking, fragile glass)
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1518_Task10" name="Post-installation follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-installation follow-up: (a) Project Estimator contacts customer 30–60 days after installation to verify system performance; (b) if customer reports underperformance: coordinates troubleshooting with installation partner and Category Manager (Electrical); (c) collects customer testimonial and performance data for future ROI model calibration
Responsible (R): Project Estimator
Accountable (A): Category Manager (Electrical)
Duration: 10–15 min/follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1518_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1518_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1518_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1518_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-267 (ensure controlled execution — Project Estimation &amp; Advisory (PA-09.2).) | - operational: design requires electrical engineering knowledge that most store associates do not possess
Owner: Project Estimator (Electrical)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1518_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1518_Annotation12" targetRef="W1518_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
